// The console's server: accounts, sessions and verified leaderboards, for every wrela game
// (games/capybara/design.md, "Accounts and leaderboards"). The console's program runs it as its
// server build, on Cloudflare (toolchain 0.13.0's host: a Durable Object holds the instance and its
// store), answering HTTP requests to wrela.dev's `/api/` (wire.wrela). A game reaches it only through
// the console (link.wrela), since a server takes only its own program's clients
// (docs/toolchain-gaps.md, "A server takes one program's clients").
//
// It is a state machine over its host, so tests can run it on a fake store: what it asks of the
// host comes out as `Command`s (the store's reads and writes, random bytes, a signature to check,
// the responses), and the host's answers go back in by their ticket (`answer`). The console's
// `serve` (console_server) carries the commands out through std::store, std::crypto and std::http,
// one call at a time; a read is answered on the call after the one that asked, and the host commits
// a call's writes when it returns, before its responses go.
//
// **A request is a short connection**: it opens, gives its one request (`http`), and takes one
// response. Every request is answered: one whose work ends without a reply is refused at the end of
// the call (`end`). Its session is the `__Host-session` cookie, read again on each request.
//
// What it keeps is in the store (account.wrela's keys), never only in memory: the host may drop the
// instance between requests, and does after a failed call. A ceremony's challenge is kept in the
// store too, under the token of the browser that asked for it (its `__Host-ceremony` cookie), so it
// is used once, by that browser. In memory are only what may be lost: the requests under way, which
// ceremonies and names were used in calls whose writes a read may not yet see, a limit on recovery
// tries across everyone (the host limits each client: docs/toolchain.md), the run being verified, and
// which requests wait for their uploads.
//
// **Passkeys** (WebAuthn Level 3, §7, through std::webauthn; the signature through std::crypto):
// every check the design asks for. A credential belongs to one account; an assertion is taken only
// for its credential's account, and with the account's handle when the browser gives one.
//
// **Runs** are verified by playing them again on the board's build (the game's `Game`): the server
// works out the time and the category itself, and refuses a run whose claim the rules can't make.
// An upload is bounded (its bytes, its ticks, an account's runs an hour, the queue's length), and
// the queue plays one run at a time, `PLAY_TICKS` ticks a call, so a run an attacker chose holds up
// the server's other requests a bounded time each call. The queue is in the store, so it goes on
// after the instance is dropped; the upload's request is answered when its run is.
//
// **Agreement** is recorded, never assumed: an account is made only with the current Terms and
// Privacy Policy agreed to and its player 13 or older, and a run is posted only once the account
// has agreed to what posting makes public (`Versions`, which the console's build gives). Each is
// kept with its version and its time.
//
// **The public reads** (a board's page, a slice of one, a run's replay, a search of names) answer
// everyone the same, so the host's cache keeps them (`BOARD_AGE`, `RUN_AGE`, `REPLAY_AGE`): they
// read no session, though the browser sends its cookie with them, and set no cookie. They
// show nothing a board doesn't: a search finds only names with runs on the boards, and a replay is
// found only by its hash, which a board's page gives. Each reads a bounded number of entries.
//
// **The clock** is the host's wall clock: each request's time (`Asked::time`), never going back
// while the instance runs. Work no request waits on (the queue) needs no time.

use account::{
    Account, Agreement, CHALLENGE_BYTES, CHALLENGE_LIFE, CODES, CODE_BYTES, CSRF_BYTES, FRESH,
    GameToken, HANDLE_BYTES, HOUR, MINUTE, MOST_PASSKEYS, OF_AGREED, OF_BEST, OF_CODE, OF_HOUR,
    OF_PASSKEY, OF_POSTING, OF_POST_BEST, OF_REPLAY, OF_RUN, OF_SESSION, OF_TOKEN, Passkey,
    PostBest, Posting, REROLLS, Recovery, SESSION_LIFE, Session, TOKEN_BYTES, TOKEN_LIFE,
    account_key, agreement_key, ceremonies, ceremony_key, code, code_hash, code_key, hashed,
    indexed, name_key, passkey_key, post_best_key, posted_key, posting_key, public_id, session_key,
    token_key, u32_at, u64_at, under_account, with_bytes, CEREMONY_BYTES,
}
use names::{Matching, Name, draw}
use std::collections::replace
use std::crypto::{Signature, verified}
use std::fmt::json_text
use std::hash::sha256::hex
use std::serialize::{LoadError, Serialize, load, save}
use std::store::{append_u32, append_u64, entries, past, value}
use std::webauthn::{Credential, Expected, assertion, base64url, registration}
use wire::{
    ADD_PASSKEY, ANY, AROUND, Agreed, BOARD_PAGE, EXPORT_PART, FULL, Found, MOST_FOUND, MOST_PART,
    MOST_REPLAY, Me, NOT_AGREED, PasskeyView, Place, REGISTER, Reply, Request, SIGN_IN, SessionView,
    Standing, WHOLE, public,
}

// ---- what a game gives the server ----------------------------------------------------------------

/// What a replay says it is, read without playing it: its course and its time in ticks.
pub struct Claim: Copy {
    pub course: u32,
    pub ticks: u32,
}

/// What playing a replay made of it: its time, and whether it counts for 100%.
pub struct Outcome: Copy {
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub full: bool,
}

/// A game's boards: its name, its board's version (its build of play: a change to play starts a
/// new one, games/capybara/design.md, "Physics is locked at release"), its courses, and how to
/// check a replay.
pub trait Game {
    /// A replay being played.
    type Run

    /// The game's key (`capybara`), as its catalog names it.
    fn id(self) -> Text

    /// The board version this build verifies for.
    fn board(self) -> u32

    /// How many courses have boards: courses 0 to this, less one.
    fn courses(self) -> u32

    /// What `replay` claims, if it reads as one of the game's replays and is within its bounds
    /// (its course, its length): `Err` says why not, for a person.
    fn claim(self, replay: [u8]) -> Result<Claim, Text>

    /// A replay that `claim` took, ready to play.
    fn start(self, replay: [u8]) -> Self::Run

    /// Plays at most `ticks` more ticks of `run`: none until it has played all of it, then what it
    /// came to, or why its claim isn't what the rules make of it.
    fn play(self, run: mut Self::Run, ticks: u32) -> Option<Result<Outcome, Text>>
}

/// The versions of what a player agrees to, as the console's build has them (console/legal.wrela):
/// the Terms and the Privacy Policy, at sign-up, and what posting makes public, before the first
/// post. The server takes only these.
pub struct Versions: Copy {
    pub terms: u32,
    pub privacy: u32,
    pub posting: u32,
}

// ---- bounds --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Runs an account may upload an hour.
pub const RUNS_AN_HOUR: u32 = 10
/// Runs waiting to be verified, and their ticks, past which an upload is refused. An upload's
/// request is answered once its run is verified, and the host gives a request 30 s: the queue's
/// ticks bound that wait (about 20 µs a tick on Cloudflare's runtime here, docs/bench.md, so about
/// 10 s), and are more than two of the longest runs a game takes.
pub const MOST_QUEUED: u32 = 32
pub const QUEUE_TICKS: u32 = 500000
/// Ticks of a run played a call. The capybara's sim took about 12 µs a tick on wrela-serve
/// (docs/bench.md, "The console's server"), so this is about 5 ms a call: the server's other
/// requests wait no longer than that behind a run, and a call stays far inside Workers Paid's CPU
/// time (30 s an invocation: developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/).
pub const PLAY_TICKS: u32 = 400
/// Recovery codes everyone may try in a minute. Each client's own limit is the host's, by address
/// (`WRELA_LIMITS`, studio/release), which the server is never told.
pub const ALL_TRIES: u32 = 30
/// How long a public read may be kept by a cache, in seconds: a board's page (it changes as runs
/// come), and a run's replay (it changes only when its account is deleted). A deleted account's
/// cached copies are gone within the longer, as the privacy policy says (console/legal.wrela).
pub const BOARD_AGE: u32 = 30
pub const RUN_AGE: u32 = 300
/// How long a replay read by its hash may be kept, in seconds: a year, as immutable. What a hash
/// names never changes; a deleted account's replay is gone from the server, though a cache may
/// still hold it for this long, as the privacy policy says.
pub const REPLAY_AGE: u32 = 31536000
/// A search's bounds: the titles and nouns' first halves it may cover together (each pair a range of
/// the index of names on the boards, `p/`, read with its title's next ones as one), the entries a
/// read of one takes, the entries it reads in all, and the names it reads the runs of, and how many
/// searches may be under way at once.
pub const MOST_RANGES: u32 = 64
pub const RANGE_PAGE: u32 = 64
pub const MOST_SCANNED: u32 = 1024
pub const MOST_CANDIDATES: u32 = 40
pub const MOST_SEARCHES: u32 = 4
/// An account's records, and its runs, read for an export at a time.
pub const EXPORT_RECORDS: u32 = 512
pub const EXPORT_RUNS: u32 = 64
/// Expired ceremonies cleared as a new one begins.
pub const PRUNED: u32 = 16
/// The most places a run's place is counted to.
pub const MOST_PLACE: u32 = 1000

// ---- what the server asks of its host ------------------------------------------------------------

pub enum Command: Clone {
    Get { ticket: u32, key: Vec<u8> },
    Scan { ticket: u32, from: Vec<u8>, to: Vec<u8>, limit: u32, down: bool },
    Put { key: Vec<u8>, value: Vec<u8> },
    Delete { key: Vec<u8> },
    Random { ticket: u32, n: u32 },
    Verify {
        ticket: u32,
        algorithm: Signature,
        key: Vec<u8>,
        message: Vec<u8>,
        signature: Vec<u8>,
    },
    /// The one answer to request `conn`: a `Reply`'s bytes, the cookies it sets, how long a cache
    /// may keep it (0: none may), and whether it never changes.
    Respond { conn: u32, body: Vec<u8>, cookies: Vec<Cookie>, public: u32, immutable: bool },
}

/// A first-party session cookie (`std::http::session_cookie`): `__Host-<name>`, holding `value`,
/// for `max_age` seconds (0 clears it).
pub struct Cookie: Clone {
    pub name: String,
    pub value: Vec<u8>,
    pub max_age: u32,
}

/// The session's and a ceremony's cookies.
pub const SESSION: Text = "session"
pub const CEREMONY: Text = "ceremony"

/// A request, as the host gave it: when it was taken (the host's wall clock, milliseconds since the
/// Unix epoch), whether it may be cached (a `GET`), its cookies' values, and its body (a `Request`).
pub struct Asked: Clone {
    pub time: u64,
    pub public: bool,
    pub session: Vec<u8>,
    pub ceremony: Vec<u8>,
    pub body: Vec<u8>,
}

// ---- records of runs -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// A verified run (`u/<run>`): whose, which board, its course, time and categories, and its
/// replay.
pub struct Run: Clone + Serialize {
    pub id: u64,
    pub account: u64,
    pub game: String,
    pub board: u32,
    pub course: u32,
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub full: bool,
    pub uploaded: u64,
    pub replay: Vec<u8>,
}

/// A run waiting to be verified (`q/<uploaded>/<run>`), and who to tell.
pub struct Queued: Clone + Serialize {
    pub id: u64,
    pub account: u64,
    pub name: String,
    pub game: String,
    pub board: u32,
    pub course: u32,
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub uploaded: u64,
    pub replay: Vec<u8>,
}

/// An account's best on a board (`a/<id>/b<board key>`): the run, its time, the board's key that
/// ranks it, to replace it, and its replay's hash (empty for a whole game's).
pub struct Best: Clone + Serialize {
    pub run: u64,
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub ranked: Vec<u8>,
    pub replay: Vec<u8>,
}

/// A place on a board's ranking (`b/...`): the name it shows, the run to watch and its replay's
/// hash (empty for a whole game's).
pub struct Ranked: Clone + Serialize {
    pub name: String,
    pub run: u64,
    pub replay: Vec<u8>,
}

/// A best and a place as they were kept before replays had hashes: read as one with none.
struct BestBefore: Clone + Serialize {
    run: u64,
    ticks: u32,
    ranked: Vec<u8>,
}

struct RankedBefore: Clone + Serialize {
    name: String,
    run: u64,
}

fn best_of(bytes: [u8]) -> Option<Best> {
    if let Some(b) = read::<Best>(bytes) {
        return Some(b)
    }
    let b = read::<BestBefore>(bytes)?
    Some(Best { run: b.run, ticks: b.ticks, ranked: b.ranked.clone(), replay: Vec::new() })
}

fn ranked_of(bytes: [u8]) -> Option<Ranked> {
    if let Some(r) = read::<Ranked>(bytes) {
        return Some(r)
    }
    let r = read::<RankedBefore>(bytes)?
    Some(Ranked { name: r.name.clone(), run: r.run, replay: Vec::new() })
}

/// What an account's index entry of a run holds (`a/<id>/u<run>`): enough to show it in an export
/// without its replay.
pub struct RunIndex: Clone + Serialize {
    pub game: String,
    pub board: u32,
    pub course: u32,
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub full: bool,
    pub uploaded: u64,
}

fn text_key(p: Text) -> Vec<u8> {
    Vec::from(String::from(p).as_bytes())
}

fn push_text(k: mut Vec<u8>, s: str) {
    for i in 0..s.len() {
        k.push(s.byte(i))
    }
    k.push(0)
}

/// `u/<run>`: a run.
pub fn run_key(id: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = text_key("u/")
    append_u64(mut k, id)
    k
}

/// What came of an upload: its run waiting to be played, verified (on board version `board`, its
/// course and time), or rejected, and why.
pub enum Checked: Clone + Serialize {
    Waiting,
    Verified { board: u32, course: u32, ticks: u32 },
    Rejected { why: String },
}

/// A replay uploaded, by its SHA-256 (`h/<hash>`): the account that uploaded it first, as run
/// `run`, and what came of it. It is claimed as the upload is let into the queue, one record a
/// hash, so a replay names one run: another account's copy of it is refused, and its own account's
/// upload of it again hears what came of the first. The account keeps an index entry of it
/// (`a/<id>/v<hash>`), so deleting the account deletes the hashes it claimed, and no other's.
pub struct Uploaded: Clone + Serialize {
    pub account: u64,
    pub run: u64,
    pub checked: Checked,
}

/// `h/<hash>`: the upload whose replay's SHA-256 is `hash` (`Uploaded`).
pub fn replay_key(hash: [u8]) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = text_key("h/")
    with_bytes(mut k, hash)
    k
}

/// `q/`: the queue, oldest first.
pub fn queue_prefix() -> Vec<u8> {
    text_key("q/")
}

pub fn queue_key(at: u64, id: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = queue_prefix()
    append_u64(mut k, at)
    append_u64(mut k, id)
    k
}

/// `x/`: the accounts being deleted.
pub fn deletions() -> Vec<u8> {
    text_key("x/")
}

/// `x/<id>`: account `id` is being deleted, until every record of it is gone.
pub fn deletion_key(id: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = deletions()
    append_u64(mut k, id)
    k
}

/// What a board is: its game, version, course (or `WHOLE`) and category, as key bytes.
pub fn board_part(game: str, board: u32, course: u32, category: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
    push_text(mut k, game)
    append_u32(mut k, board)
    append_u32(mut k, course)
    append_u32(mut k, category)
    k
}

/// `b/<board>`: a board's ranking, fastest first: `b/<board><ticks><account>`.
pub fn board_prefix(game: str, board: u32, course: u32, category: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = text_key("b/")
    for b in board_part(game, board, course, category) {
        k.push(b)
    }
    k
}

pub fn ranked_key(
    game: str,
    board: u32,
    course: u32,
    category: u32,
    ticks: u32,
    account: u64,
) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = board_prefix(game, board, course, category)
    append_u32(mut k, ticks)
    append_u64(mut k, account)
    k
}

/// `a/<id>/b<board>`: an account's best on a board.
pub fn best_key(account: u64, game: str, board: u32, course: u32, category: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    indexed(account, OF_BEST, board_part(game, board, course, category))
}

/// `a/<id>/b<game><version>`: the start of an account's bests on one version of a game's boards.
pub fn bests_prefix(account: u64, game: str, board: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var rest: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
    push_text(mut rest, game)
    append_u32(mut rest, board)
    indexed(account, OF_BEST, rest)
}

/// `a/<id>/h<hour>`: an account's uploads in an hour of the server's clock.
pub fn rate_key(account: u64, hour: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    var rest: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
    append_u64(mut rest, hour)
    indexed(account, OF_HOUR, rest)
}

// ---- the server's state ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// A ceremony a browser began (`w/...`): its challenge, and for a new account, what it will be.
struct Ceremony: Clone + Serialize {
    kind: u32,
    challenge: Vec<u8>,
    handle: Vec<u8>,
    account: u64,
    seed: u64,
    expires: u64,
    agreed: Agreed,
}

/// A request, and the session its cookie is for.
struct Conn: Clone {
    conn: u32,
    /// Whether it was answered, and whether its answer may be cached.
    answered: bool,
    public: bool,
    /// The session's token's hash: empty when signed out.
    session: Vec<u8>,
    account: u64,
    csrf: Vec<u8>,
    fresh_until: u64,
    recovery: bool,
    /// Its ceremony cookie's value, and the cookies its response sets.
    ceremony: Vec<u8>,
    cookies: Vec<Cookie>,
    /// The run its upload waits for (0: none; a run's number never is).
    run: u64,
}

/// What a job waits for.
enum Step: Copy + Eq {
    HelloSession,
    HelloAccount,
    BeginRandom,
    BeginPrune,
    CeremonyTaken,
    BeginAddScan,
    BeginAddAccount,
    RegisterCredential,
    RegisterAccount,
    RegisterName,
    RegisterSeed,
    RegisterSecrets,
    SignInCredential,
    SignInAccount,
    SignInVerify,
    SignInSecrets,
    RecoverCode,
    RecoverAccount,
    RecoverSessions,
    RecoverSecrets,
    NameAccount,
    NameSeed,
    NameTaken,
    AddCredential,
    AddCount,
    AddSession,
    RemoveScan,
    PasskeysScan,
    CodesScan,
    CodesRandom,
    SessionsScan,
    RevokeScan,
    TokenAccount,
    TokenPrune,
    TokenRandom,
    QueueAccount,
    ExportAccount,
    DeleteResume,
    ExportScan,
    ExportRuns,
    ExportRun,
    DeleteAccount,
    DeleteScan,
    DeleteNext,
    UploadToken,
    UploadAccount,
    UploadRate,
    UploadClaim,
    UploadPlace,
    UploadQueue,
    UploadId,
    BoardScan,
    WatchRun,
    PostingRead,
    PostingBest,
    BestRunsRead,
    UploadConsent,
    ReplayIndex,
    ReplayRun,
    AroundName,
    AroundBest,
    AroundAbove,
    AroundBelow,
    AroundCount,
    NamesRange,
    NamesAccount,
    FinishBest,
    FinishBests,
    FinishPlace,
}

/// A request under way, waiting on its ticket: what it has learned so far.
struct Job: Clone {
    conn: u32,
    /// The call it began in: a key deleted since may have been read by it before the delete
    /// committed (`gone`).
    since: u64,
    /// The call its last read (`get`) was asked in: the store it answers from is as of before that
    /// call's writes.
    asked: u64,
    ticket: u32,
    step: Step,
    request: Request,
    account: Option<Account>,
    passkey: Option<Passkey>,
    session: Option<Session>,
    credential: Option<Credential>,
    message: Vec<u8>,
    hash: Vec<u8>,
    keys: Vec<Vec<u8>>,
    views: Vec<Vec<u8>>,
    text: String,
    id: u64,
    seed: u64,
    tries: u32,
    n: u32,
    queued: Option<Queued>,
    categories: Vec<u32>,
    category: u32,
    /// What a new account agreed to, from its ceremony.
    agreed: Agreed,
    /// The parts a search's names may have, worked out once for its every page.
    matching: Option<Matching>,
}

/// A search whose candidates' runs are being read, all at once: what it found, each with its
/// candidate's place in the index's order, and how many reads are still to come.
struct Search: Clone {
    conn: u32,
    found: Vec<(u32, Found)>,
    left: u32,
}

/// A replay's hash claimed by an upload lately (`Uploaded`), by `account` as run `run`, in call
/// `call`: a read made before that call's writes commit doesn't see it.
struct Claiming: Clone {
    hash: Vec<u8>,
    call: u64,
    account: u64,
    run: u64,
}

/// The run being verified.
struct Verifying<R> {
    key: Vec<u8>,
    queued: Queued,
    run: R,
}

/// The server.
pub struct Engine<G: Game> {
    game: G,
    rp_id: String,
    origin: String,
    versions: Versions,
    out: Vec<Command>,
    ticket: u32,
    /// The server's clock: the latest request's time, in milliseconds since the Unix epoch.
    now: u64,
    conns: Vec<Conn>,
    jobs: Vec<Job>,
    /// When anyone tried a recovery code, within a minute.
    tries: Vec<u64>,
    /// The queue may hold runs; the ticket of a scan for the oldest.
    queue_waiting: bool,
    queue_scan: Option<u32>,
    /// The calls counted, and the last that wrote the queue: a read made in a call is answered
    /// from the store as it was before the call's writes (wrela_host::server), so the queue is
    /// read again only in a later call.
    call: u64,
    queue_written: u64,
    /// Names written, and single-use or revocable keys deleted (ceremonies, sessions, recovery
    /// codes, passkeys), lately: a read made before their call committed wouldn't see them so
    /// (docs/toolchain-gaps.md, "A call's reads don't see its writes").
    recent_names: Vec<(Vec<u8>, u64)>,
    gone: Vec<(Vec<u8>, u64)>,
    /// The accounts whose records a job wrote lately (a run's upload, verification or ranking),
    /// which a deletion's scan made before the write committed wouldn't see.
    touched: Vec<(u64, u64)>,
    /// Uploads let into the queue lately (the call, and the run's ticks), which a scan of the queue
    /// made before their call committed wouldn't count.
    admitted: Vec<(u64, u32)>,
    /// Replays' hashes claimed lately, and runs whose outcome was written lately (the run, the
    /// call): a read made before their call committed wouldn't see them.
    claims: Vec<Claiming>,
    finished: Vec<(u64, u64)>,
    /// The searches reading their candidates.
    searching: Vec<Search>,
    /// Whether deletions a dropped instance left may wait (`x/`), and the call that last finished one.
    deletions_waiting: bool,
    deletion_written: u64,
    verifying: Option<Verifying<G::Run>>,
    /// Whether the last call asked for nothing: then nothing would call it again, so a run being
    /// played asks the host for a byte to be called at once.
    nudge: Option<u32>,
}

/// A server for `game`'s boards, its passkeys for relying party `rp_id` from `origin` alone, taking
/// the agreements of `versions`.
pub fn engine<G: Game>(game: take G, rp_id: str, origin: str, versions: Versions) -> Engine<G> {
    Engine {
        game,
        rp_id: rp_id.to_string(),
        origin: origin.to_string(),
        versions,
        out: Vec::new(),
        ticket: 0,
        now: 0,
        conns: Vec::new(),
        jobs: Vec::new(),
        tries: Vec::new(),
        queue_waiting: true,
        queue_scan: None,
        call: 0,
        queue_written: 0,
        recent_names: Vec::new(),
        gone: Vec::new(),
        touched: Vec::new(),
        admitted: Vec::new(),
        claims: Vec::new(),
        finished: Vec::new(),
        searching: Vec::new(),
        deletions_waiting: true,
        deletion_written: 0,
        verifying: None,
        nudge: None,
    }
}

fn blank_job(conn: u32, request: take Request) -> Job {
    Job {
        conn,
        since: 0,
        asked: 0,
        ticket: 0,
        step: Step::HelloSession,
        request,
        account: None,
        passkey: None,
        session: None,
        credential: None,
        message: Vec::new(),
        hash: Vec::new(),
        keys: Vec::new(),
        views: Vec::new(),
        text: String::new(),
        id: 0,
        seed: 0,
        tries: 0,
        n: 0,
        queued: None,
        categories: Vec::new(),
        category: 0,
        agreed: NOT_AGREED,
        matching: None,
    }
}

fn me_of(a: Account, recovery: bool) -> Me {
    Me {
        signed_in: true,
        name: names::text(a.name),
        fixed: a.fixed,
        rerolls: a.rerolls,
        must_add_passkey: recovery,
    }
}

fn nobody() -> Me {
    Me { signed_in: false, name: String::new(), fixed: false, rerolls: 0, must_add_passkey: false }
}

fn read<T: Serialize>(bytes: [u8]) -> Option<T> {
    let r: Result<T, LoadError> = load(Vec::from(bytes))
    take r.ok()
}

/// The value a `get` answered with, as a `T`: none for no value, or one that doesn't read.
fn got<T: Serialize>(answer: [u8]) -> Option<T> {
    let v = value(answer)?
    read(v)
}

/// The bytes from `at`, `n` of them.
fn part(bytes: [u8], at: u32, n: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var out: Vec<u8> = Vec::with_capacity(n)
    for i in at..at + n {
        out.push(bytes[i])
    }
    out
}

fn same_bytes(a: [u8], b: [u8]) -> bool {
    if a.len() != b.len() {
        return false
    }
    // Every byte is compared, whatever the first that differs, so the time says nothing of where.
    var d: u32 = 0
    for i in 0..a.len() {
        d = d | u32(a[i] ^ b[i])
    }
    d == 0
}

impl<G: Game> Engine<G> {
    // ---- the host's side --------------------------------------------------------------------

    /// Starts a call.
    pub fn begin(mut self) {
        self.call += 1
    }

    /// Ends a call: the queue's work, then a refusal for each request whose work ended unanswered,
    /// so none waits for the host's timeout.
    pub fn end(mut self) {
        self.verify_some()
        self.resume_deletions()
        self.forget_old()
        var left: Vec<u32> = Vec::new()
        for c in self.conns {
            if !c.answered && !self.busy(c) {
                left.push(c.conn)
            }
        }
        for conn in left {
            self.refuse(conn, "Something went wrong on our end. Try again in a moment.")
        }
    }

    /// Request `conn` closed (answered, or its client went): its jobs finish their writes, and an
    /// upload it waited for is verified all the same.
    pub fn closed(mut self, conn: u32) {
        self.conns.retain(|c| c.conn != conn)
    }

    /// Request `conn`'s request: read its session from its cookie, if it has one, then do it.
    pub fn http(mut self, conn: u32, asked: Asked) {
        self.closed(conn)
        self.conns.push(
            Conn {
                conn,
                answered: false,
                public: asked.public,
                session: Vec::new(),
                account: 0,
                csrf: Vec::new(),
                fresh_until: 0,
                recovery: false,
                ceremony: asked.ceremony.clone(),
                cookies: Vec::new(),
                run: 0,
            },
        )
        self.now = max(self.now, asked.time)
        let parsed: Option<Request> = read(asked.body)
        let Some(request) = take parsed else {
            self.refuse(conn, "wrela.dev can't read that request. Reload the page and try again.")
            return
        }
        if asked.public && !public(request) {
            self.refuse(conn, "That request changes things, so it can't be a GET.")
            return
        }
        // The public reads and an upload (by a game's token) are no session's.
        if sessionless(request) || asked.session.is_empty() {
            self.request(conn, take request)
            return
        }
        var job = blank_job(conn, take request)
        if asked.session.len() != TOKEN_BYTES {
            self.no_session(take job)
            return
        }
        job.hash = hashed(asked.session)
        let k = session_key(job.hash)
        self.get(take k, Step::HelloSession, take job)
    }

    /// The host's answer to ticket `ticket`: its bytes, or none if the request failed.
    pub fn answer(mut self, ticket: u32, answer: Option<Vec<u8>>) {
        if self.nudge == Some(ticket) {
            self.nudge = None
            return
        }
        if self.queue_scan == Some(ticket) {
            self.queue_scan = None
            self.queue_answered(answer)
            return
        }
        var found: Option<u32> = None
        for i in 0..self.jobs.len() {
            if self.jobs[i].ticket == ticket {
                found = Some(i)
            }
        }
        let Some(i) = found else { return }
        let job = self.jobs.remove(i)
        if job.step == Step::QueueAccount {
            self.queue_scan = None
        }
        match answer {
            Some(bytes) => self.advance(take job, bytes),
            None => {
                // A run's ranking can't finish: its upload hears so. A deletion's mark stays, and
                // the next call takes it up again.
                if let Some(q) = job.queued {
                    let why = String::from(
                        "We couldn't finish checking that run. Try again later.",
                    )
                    self.tell(q.id, Reply::Refused { why })
                }
                if is_deletion(job.step) {
                    self.deletions_waiting = true
                    self.deletion_written = self.call
                }
                if job.step == Step::NamesAccount {
                    self.searching.retain(|s| s.conn != job.conn)
                }
                self.refuse(
                    job.conn,
                    "Something went wrong on our end. Try again in a moment.",
                )
            },
        }
    }

    /// What the server asks of its host, since the last time.
    pub fn commands(mut self) -> Vec<Command> {
        replace(mut self.out, Vec::new())
    }

    // ---- helpers ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn next_ticket(mut self) -> u32 {
        self.ticket += 1
        self.ticket
    }

    fn conn_index(self, conn: u32) -> Option<u32> {
        for i in 0..self.conns.len() {
            if self.conns[i].conn == conn {
                return Some(i)
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// Whether request `c` still has work under way: a job (its session being read among them), or
    /// an upload being verified.
    fn busy(self, c: Conn) -> bool {
        if c.run != 0 {
            return true
        }
        for j in self.jobs {
            if j.conn == c.conn {
                return true
            }
        }
        false
    }

    /// Answers request `conn` with `reply`, once: a public read's answer may be cached.
    fn reply(mut self, conn: u32, reply: take Reply) {
        let age = match reply {
            Reply::Board { .. } | Reply::Around { .. } | Reply::Unplaced | Reply::Names { .. } => {
                BOARD_AGE
            },
            Reply::Run { .. } => RUN_AGE,
            _ => 0,
        }
        self.respond(conn, take reply, age, immutable: false)
    }

    /// Answers request `conn` with `reply`, once, which a cache may keep `age` seconds if it was a
    /// public read (a `GET`), as never changing if `immutable`.
    fn respond(mut self, conn: u32, reply: take Reply, age: u32, immutable: bool) {
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return }
        if self.conns[i].answered {
            return
        }
        self.conns[i].answered = true
        let public = if self.conns[i].public { age } else { 0 }
        let cookies = self.conns[i].cookies.clone()
        self.out.push(
            Command::Respond {
                conn,
                body: save(reply),
                cookies,
                public,
                immutable: immutable && public > 0,
            },
        )
    }

    fn refuse(mut self, conn: u32, why: Text) {
        self.reply(conn, Reply::Refused { why: String::from(why) })
    }

    /// Answers request `conn` with its account as `me`, and its session's CSRF token.
    fn welcome(mut self, conn: u32, me: take Me) {
        let csrf = match self.conn_index(conn) {
            Some(i) => self.conns[i].csrf.clone(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        }
        self.reply(conn, Reply::Welcome { me, csrf })
    }

    /// Answers the requests that wait for run `run`, if any still do: its upload, and the same
    /// replay's uploads again while it waited.
    fn tell(mut self, run: u64, reply: take Reply) {
        var waiting: Vec<u32> = Vec::new()
        for i in 0..self.conns.len() {
            if self.conns[i].run == run {
                self.conns[i].run = 0
                waiting.push(self.conns[i].conn)
            }
        }
        for conn in waiting {
            self.reply(conn, reply.clone())
        }
    }

    /// Sets cookie `name` on request `conn`'s response (`value` empty and `max_age` 0 clear it).
    fn cookie(mut self, conn: u32, name: Text, value: take Vec<u8>, max_age: u32) {
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return }
        self.conns[i].cookies.push(Cookie { name: String::from(name), value, max_age })
    }

    /// Request `conn`'s session cookie is for no session (any more): it is cleared.
    fn session_gone(mut self, conn: u32) {
        self.cookie(conn, SESSION, Vec::new(), 0)
    }

    /// `job`'s session cookie is for no session: cleared, and its request goes on signed out.
    fn no_session(mut self, job: take Job) {
        self.session_gone(job.conn)
        self.request(job.conn, job.request.clone())
    }

    /// Waits on `job`'s ticket, from the call it began in.
    fn push_job(mut self, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        if j.since == 0 {
            j.since = self.call
        }
        self.jobs.push(take j)
    }

    fn get(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>, step: Step, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Get { ticket: t, key })
        j.ticket = t
        j.asked = self.call
        j.step = step
        self.push_job(take j)
    }

    /// The last `limit` entries from `from` to before `to`, the last first.
    fn scan_down(
        mut self,
        from: take Vec<u8>,
        to: take Vec<u8>,
        limit: u32,
        step: Step,
        job: take Job,
    ) {
        var j = take job
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Scan { ticket: t, from, to, limit, down: true })
        j.ticket = t
        j.step = step
        self.push_job(take j)
    }

    fn scan(mut self, from: take Vec<u8>, limit: u32, step: Step, job: take Job) {
        let to = past(from).unwrap_or(Vec::new())
        self.scan_range(take from, take to, limit, step, take job)
    }

    fn scan_range(
        mut self,
        from: take Vec<u8>,
        to: take Vec<u8>,
        limit: u32,
        step: Step,
        job: take Job,
    ) {
        var j = take job
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Scan { ticket: t, from, to, limit, down: false })
        j.ticket = t
        j.step = step
        self.push_job(take j)
    }

    fn random(mut self, n: u32, step: Step, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Random { ticket: t, n })
        j.ticket = t
        j.step = step
        self.push_job(take j)
    }

    fn put<T: Serialize>(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>, record: T) {
        self.out.push(Command::Put { key, value: save(record) })
    }

    fn put_bytes(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>, value: take Vec<u8>) {
        self.out.push(Command::Put { key, value })
    }

    fn delete(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>) {
        self.out.push(Command::Delete { key })
    }

    /// Deletes `key`, a single-use or revocable record, and remembers it gone: a read of it made
    /// before this call's writes commit is not to be trusted.
    fn forget(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>) {
        self.gone.push((key.clone(), self.call))
        self.delete(take key)
    }

    /// The request's account, if it is signed in with a session whose CSRF token is `csrf`
    /// (none: no token asked for), and a passkey session unless `recovery` allows one made by a
    /// code; a refusal said if not.
    fn signed_in(mut self, conn: u32, csrf: Option<Vec<u8>>, recovery: bool) -> Option<Conn> {
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return None }
        let c = self.conns[i].clone()
        if c.session.is_empty() {
            self.refuse(conn, "Sign in first.")
            return None
        }
        if let Some(token) = csrf {
            if !same_bytes(token, c.csrf) {
                self.refuse(conn, "That request didn't come from this console. Reload the page.")
                return None
            }
        }
        if c.recovery && !recovery {
            self.refuse(conn, "You signed in with a recovery code. Add a passkey first.")
            return None
        }
        Some(c)
    }

    /// Like `signed_in`, and the sign-in fresh: within `FRESH` of a passkey's, or by a code.
    fn fresh(mut self, conn: u32, csrf: Vec<u8>, recovery: bool) -> Option<Conn> {
        let c = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery)?
        if !c.recovery && c.fresh_until < self.now {
            self.refuse(
                conn,
                "This needs a fresh sign-in. Sign in with your passkey again first.",
            )
            return None
        }
        Some(c)
    }

    /// Takes the ceremony that request `conn`'s cookie names, of the kind `job`'s request finishes,
    /// then goes on with `job` (`CeremonyTaken`); refused if it has none, or one that has expired
    /// or was used. It is used up whatever comes of it: deleted, and its cookie cleared.
    fn take_ceremony(mut self, conn: u32, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        let kind = match j.request {
            Request::Register { .. } => REGISTER,
            Request::SignIn { .. } => SIGN_IN,
            _ => ADD_PASSKEY,
        }
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return }
        let v = self.conns[i].ceremony.clone()
        if v.len() != 8 + CEREMONY_BYTES {
            self.refuse(conn, expired(kind))
            return
        }
        let expires = u64_at(v, 0)
        let key = ceremony_key(expires, hashed(part(v, 8, CEREMONY_BYTES)))
        self.cookie(conn, CEREMONY, Vec::new(), 0)
        if expires < self.now || lately(self.gone, key) {
            self.refuse(conn, expired(kind))
            return
        }
        // Used now: a read made before this call's delete commits would still find it.
        self.forget(key.clone())
        j.n = kind
        self.get(take key, Step::CeremonyTaken, take j)
    }

    /// Why a new account can't be made with `agreed`, if it can't: it must agree to the current
    /// Terms and Privacy Policy, and its player be 13 or older.
    fn disagreed(self, agreed: Agreed) -> Option<Text> {
        if !agreed.of_age {
            return Some("You need to be 13 or older to make an account.")
        }
        if agreed.terms == 0 || agreed.privacy == 0 {
            return Some("Agree to the Terms and the Privacy Policy to make an account.")
        }
        if agreed.terms != self.versions.terms || agreed.privacy != self.versions.privacy {
            return Some(
                "The Terms or the Privacy Policy changed since this page loaded. Reload the page and read them again.",
            )
        }
        None
    }

    /// Whether `game` has a board for `course` (or WHOLE) and `category` here.
    fn board_known(self, game: str, course: u32, category: u32) -> bool {
        game == self.game.id() &&
            (course < self.game.courses() || course == WHOLE) &&
            (category == ANY || category == FULL)
    }

    /// Whether agreement `p` (none: never agreed) is to the current version of what posting makes
    /// public.
    fn agreed_to(self, p: Option<Posting>) -> bool {
        match p {
            Some(p) => p.version == self.versions.posting,
            None => false,
        }
    }

    /// The searches of names under way: reading the index, or their candidates.
    fn searches(self) -> u32 {
        var n = self.searching.len()
        for j in self.jobs {
            if j.step == Step::NamesRange {
                n += 1
            }
        }
        n
    }

    fn is_signed_in(self, conn: u32) -> bool {
        match self.conn_index(conn) {
            Some(i) => !self.conns[i].session.is_empty(),
            None => false,
        }
    }

    fn expected(self, challenge: Vec<u8>) -> Expected {
        Expected {
            rp_id: self.rp_id.clone(),
            origin: self.origin.clone(),
            challenge: challenge.clone(),
        }
    }

    /// Binds connection `conn` to a session.
    fn bind(mut self, conn: u32, hash: Vec<u8>, s: Session) {
        if let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) {
            self.conns[i].session = hash.clone()
            self.conns[i].account = s.account
            self.conns[i].csrf = s.csrf.clone()
            self.conns[i].fresh_until = s.fresh_until
            self.conns[i].recovery = s.recovery
        }
    }

    /// Lets go of every request's binding to the session `hash` (every session, if empty) of
    /// `account`: a request under way of a session that ended is no longer signed in.
    fn unbind(mut self, account: u64, hash: Vec<u8>) {
        for i in 0..self.conns.len() {
            let c = self.conns[i].clone()
            if c.account == account &&
                !c.session.is_empty() &&
                (hash.is_empty() || same_bytes(c.session, hash)) {
                self.conns[i].session = Vec::new()
                self.conns[i].account = 0
                self.conns[i].csrf = Vec::new()
                self.conns[i].recovery = false
            }
        }
    }

    /// Writes a new session for `account` from `secrets` (its token, then its CSRF token), binds
    /// request `conn` to it, sets its cookie, and answers with it.
    fn begin_session(
        mut self,
        conn: u32,
        a: Account,
        secrets: [u8],
        recovery: bool,
        codes: Vec<String>,
    ) {
        let token = part(secrets, 0, TOKEN_BYTES)
        let csrf = part(secrets, TOKEN_BYTES, CSRF_BYTES)
        let hash = hashed(token)
        // The session this browser had ends: its cookie is replaced, so nothing could use it again.
        if let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) {
            let old = self.conns[i].session.clone()
            let owner = self.conns[i].account
            if !old.is_empty() {
                self.forget(session_key(old))
                self.delete(indexed(owner, OF_SESSION, old))
            }
        }
        let s = Session {
            account: a.id,
            csrf: csrf.clone(),
            created: self.now,
            seen: self.now,
            fresh_until: self.now + FRESH,
            recovery,
        }
        self.put(session_key(hash), s.clone())
        self.put(
            indexed(a.id, OF_SESSION, hash),
            SessionView { id: public_id(hash), created: self.now, seen: self.now, this: false },
        )
        self.bind(conn, hash.clone(), s.clone())
        self.cookie(conn, SESSION, take token, u32(SESSION_LIFE / 1000))
        self.reply(conn, Reply::Session { csrf, me: me_of(a, recovery), codes: codes.clone() })
    }

    /// Writes recovery codes for account `id` from `bytes`, and gives them as text.
    fn write_codes(mut self, id: u64, bytes: [u8]) -> Vec<String> {
        var codes: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
        for k in 0..CODES {
            let c = code(part(bytes, k * CODE_BYTES, CODE_BYTES))
            let Some(h) = code_hash(c.as_str()) else { panic("a code reads back") }
            self.put(code_key(h), Recovery { account: id })
            self.put_bytes(indexed(id, OF_CODE, h), Vec::new())
            codes.push(take c)
        }
        codes
    }

    // ---- requests -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn request(mut self, conn: u32, request: Request) {
        var job = blank_job(conn, request.clone())
        match request {
            // A session's `Me` is answered as its cookie is read (`HelloAccount`): this one has none.
            Request::Me => self.welcome(conn, nobody()),
            Request::Begin { ceremony, csrf, agreed } => {
                if ceremony == REGISTER && self.is_signed_in(conn) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Sign out first to make another account.")
                    return
                }
                if ceremony == REGISTER {
                    if let Some(why) = self.disagreed(agreed) {
                        self.refuse(conn, why)
                        return
                    }
                }
                if ceremony == REGISTER || ceremony == SIGN_IN {
                    // The challenge and the browser's token; a new account's handle, number and
                    // name come with them.
                    job.n = ceremony
                    self.random(begin_bytes(ceremony), Step::BeginRandom, take job)
                } else if ceremony == ADD_PASSKEY {
                    let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: true) else { return }
                    job.n = ceremony
                    job.id = c.account
                    self.scan(
                        indexed(c.account, OF_PASSKEY, []),
                        MOST_PASSKEYS,
                        Step::BeginAddScan,
                        take job,
                    )
                } else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That isn't a sign-in or a sign-up.")
                }
            },
            Request::Register { .. } | Request::SignIn { .. } => self.take_ceremony(conn, take job),
            Request::Recover { code } => {
                recent(mut self.tries, self.now, MINUTE)
                if self.tries.len() >= ALL_TRIES {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Too many tries. Wait a few minutes, then try again.")
                    return
                }
                self.tries.push(self.now)
                let Some(h) = code_hash(code.as_str()) else {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "That isn't a recovery code. A code has 16 letters and digits.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                job.hash = h.clone()
                self.get(code_key(h), Step::RecoverCode, take job)
            },
            Request::Reroll { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: false) else {
                    return
                }
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::NameAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::Keep { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: false) else {
                    return
                }
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::NameAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::AddPasskey { csrf, .. } => {
                let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: true) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                job.hash = c.session.clone()
                self.take_ceremony(conn, take job)
            },
            Request::RemovePasskey { csrf, id } => {
                let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: false) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                job.message = id.clone()
                self.scan(
                    indexed(c.account, OF_PASSKEY, []),
                    MOST_PASSKEYS + 1,
                    Step::RemoveScan,
                    take job,
                )
            },
            Request::Passkeys => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: true) else { return }
                self.scan(
                    indexed(c.account, OF_PASSKEY, []),
                    MOST_PASSKEYS + 1,
                    Step::PasskeysScan,
                    take job,
                )
            },
            Request::NewCodes { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: false) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                self.scan(indexed(c.account, OF_CODE, []), 4 * CODES, Step::CodesScan, take job)
            },
            Request::Sessions => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: true) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                job.hash = c.session.clone()
                self.scan(indexed(c.account, OF_SESSION, []), 256, Step::SessionsScan, take job)
            },
            Request::Revoke { csrf, session } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: true) else {
                    return
                }
                job.id = c.account
                job.hash = c.session.clone()
                job.message = session.clone()
                self.scan(indexed(c.account, OF_SESSION, []), 256, Step::RevokeScan, take job)
            },
            Request::SignOut { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: true) else {
                    return
                }
                self.forget(session_key(c.session))
                self.delete(indexed(c.account, OF_SESSION, c.session))
                self.unbind(c.account, c.session.clone())
                self.session_gone(conn)
                self.welcome(conn, nobody())
            },
            Request::Token { game } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: false) else { return }
                if game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That game has no boards on wrela.dev.")
                    return
                }
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::TokenAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::Export { after } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: true) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                job.message = after.clone()
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::ExportAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::Delete { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: false) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::DeleteAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::Upload { token, game, replay } => {
                if game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected {
                            why: String::from("That game has no boards on wrela.dev."),
                        },
                    )
                    return
                }
                if replay.len() > MOST_REPLAY || token.len() != TOKEN_BYTES {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("That run is too long to upload.") },
                    )
                    return
                }
                match self.game.claim(replay) {
                    Ok(claim) => {
                        job.category = claim.course
                        job.tries = claim.ticks
                        job.message = replay.clone()
                        self.get(token_key(hashed(token)), Step::UploadToken, take job)
                    },
                    Err(why) => self.reply(conn, Reply::Rejected { why: String::from(why) }),
                }
            },
            Request::Board { game, course, category, from } => {
                if !self.board_known(game, course, category) || from > 10000 {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That board doesn't exist.")
                    return
                }
                job.n = from
                let prefix = if course == WHOLE {
                    whole_prefix(game, self.game.board(), category)
                } else { board_prefix(game, self.game.board(), course, category) }
                self.scan(take prefix, from + BOARD_PAGE + 1, Step::BoardScan, take job)
            },
            Request::Watch { run } => {
                self.get(run_key(run), Step::WatchRun, take job)
            },
            Request::Posting => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: true) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                self.get(posting_key(c.account), Step::PostingRead, take job)
            },
            Request::Consent { csrf, version, best_runs } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: false) else {
                    return
                }
                if version != self.versions.posting {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "What a post shares has changed since this page loaded. Reload the page and read it again.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                // The agreement and the setting chosen with it, each in its own record.
                self.put(posting_key(c.account), Posting { version, at: self.now })
                self.put(post_best_key(c.account), PostBest { on: best_runs, at: self.now })
                self.touched.push((c.account, self.call))
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Posting { agreed: true, best_runs })
            },
            Request::BestRuns { csrf, on } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: false) else {
                    return
                }
                // The setting alone, written as asked: the agreement is only read, for the answer.
                self.put(post_best_key(c.account), PostBest { on, at: self.now })
                self.touched.push((c.account, self.call))
                job.id = c.account
                job.n = if on { 1 } else { 0 }
                self.get(posting_key(c.account), Step::BestRunsRead, take job)
            },
            Request::Replay { hash } => {
                if hash.len() != 32 {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That isn't a replay's hash.")
                    return
                }
                job.hash = hash.clone()
                self.get(replay_key(hash), Step::ReplayIndex, take job)
            },
            Request::Around { game, course, category, name } => {
                if !self.board_known(game, course, category) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That board doesn't exist.")
                    return
                }
                // Through the names on the boards alone (`p/`), and one answer for any name without
                // a place there, so a slice never says whether an account that never posted exists.
                let Some(n) = names::parse(name.as_str()) else {
                    self.reply(conn, Reply::Unplaced)
                    return
                }
                self.get(posted_key(n), Step::AroundName, take job)
            },
            Request::Names { game, title, noun, epithet } => {
                if game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That game has no boards on wrela.dev.")
                    return
                }
                if !searchable(title) || !searchable(noun) || !searchable(epithet) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "A name has only letters, spaces and hyphens.")
                    return
                }
                if title.is_empty() && noun.is_empty() && epithet.is_empty() {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Type part of a name to search.")
                    return
                }
                let m = names::matching(title, noun, epithet)
                if m.titles.len() * m.fronts.len() > MOST_RANGES {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Type more of the name to search. Try its title or its noun.")
                    return
                }
                if self.searches() >= MOST_SEARCHES {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Search is busy. Try again in a moment.")
                    return
                }
                // The index of names on the boards, in its order: a range for each title's run of
                // first halves one after another (all of them, for no noun: the whole title's), from
                // its first's to past its last's. `keys` holds each range's start and its end.
                for t in m.titles {
                    var k = 0
                    while k < m.fronts.len() {
                        var last = k
                        while last + 1 < m.fronts.len() &&
                            m.fronts[last + 1] == m.fronts[last] + 1 {
                            last += 1
                        }
                        job.keys.push(name_index(t, m.fronts[k]))
                        job.keys.push(name_index(t, m.fronts[last] + 1))
                        k = last + 1
                    }
                }
                if job.keys.is_empty() {
                    self.reply(conn, Reply::Names { found: Vec::new() })
                    return
                }
                job.matching = Some(take m)
                let (from, to) = (job.keys[0].clone(), job.keys[1].clone())
                self.scan_range(take from, take to, RANGE_PAGE, Step::NamesRange, take job)
            },
        }
    }

    // ---- answers ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn advance(mut self, job: take Job, answer: Vec<u8>) {
        var j = take job
        let conn = j.conn
        // A job that writes an account's runs: a deletion waits it out (`writing`).
        if is_upload(j.step) {
            self.touched.push((j.id, self.call))
        } else if let Some(q) = j.queued {
            self.touched.push((q.account, self.call))
        }
        match j.step {
            Step::HelloSession => {
                let s: Option<Session> = got(answer)
                let s = if lately(self.gone, session_key(j.hash)) { None } else { take s }
                let Some(s) = s else {
                    self.no_session(take j)
                    return
                }
                if s.created + SESSION_LIFE < self.now {
                    self.forget(session_key(j.hash))
                    self.delete(indexed(s.account, OF_SESSION, j.hash))
                    self.no_session(take j)
                    return
                }
                j.session = Some(s.clone())
                self.get(account_key(s.account), Step::HelloAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::HelloAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(s) = j.session.clone() else { return }
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    self.no_session(take j)
                    return
                }
                // Ended while it was read (signed out, revoked): it stays ended.
                if a.deleting || lately(self.gone, session_key(j.hash)) {
                    self.no_session(take j)
                    return
                }
                // When it was last seen, written at most once an hour, not with every request.
                if s.seen + HOUR < self.now {
                    var seen = s.clone()
                    seen.seen = self.now
                    self.put(session_key(j.hash), take seen)
                    self.put(
                        indexed(a.id, OF_SESSION, j.hash),
                        SessionView {
                            id: public_id(j.hash),
                            created: s.created,
                            seen: self.now,
                            this: false,
                        },
                    )
                }
                self.bind(conn, j.hash.clone(), s.clone())
                match j.request {
                    Request::Me => self.welcome(conn, me_of(a, s.recovery)),
                    _ => self.request(conn, j.request.clone()),
                }
            },
            Step::BeginRandom => {
                if answer.len() < begin_bytes(j.n) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "We couldn't start that. Try again.")
                    return
                }
                let challenge = part(answer, 0, CHALLENGE_BYTES)
                let token = part(answer, CHALLENGE_BYTES, CEREMONY_BYTES)
                let at = CHALLENGE_BYTES + CEREMONY_BYTES
                var c = Ceremony {
                    kind: j.n,
                    challenge: challenge.clone(),
                    handle: Vec::new(),
                    account: 0,
                    seed: 0,
                    expires: self.now + CHALLENGE_LIFE,
                    agreed: NOT_AGREED,
                }
                if j.n == ADD_PASSKEY {
                    c.handle = j.hash.clone()
                    c.account = j.id
                }
                if j.n == REGISTER {
                    c.handle = part(answer, at, HANDLE_BYTES)
                    c.account = u64_at(answer, at + HANDLE_BYTES)
                    c.seed = u64_at(answer, at + HANDLE_BYTES + 8)
                    if let Request::Begin { agreed, .. } = j.request {
                        c.agreed = agreed
                    }
                }
                let handle = c.handle.clone()
                // Kept under the token's hash; the browser keeps the token, and when it expires.
                var held: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
                append_u64(mut held, c.expires)
                with_bytes(mut held, token)
                self.put(ceremony_key(c.expires, hashed(token)), c.clone())
                self.cookie(conn, CEREMONY, take held, u32(CHALLENGE_LIFE / 1000))
                self.reply(
                    conn,
                    Reply::Challenge { ceremony: j.n, challenge, handle, exclude: j.keys.clone() },
                )
                // Ceremonies begun and never finished go once they expire, a few as each begins.
                var to = ceremonies()
                append_u64(mut to, self.now)
                self.scan_range(ceremonies(), take to, PRUNED, Step::BeginPrune, take j)
            },
            Step::BeginPrune => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                for e in es {
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                }
            },
            Step::CeremonyTaken => {
                let c: Option<Ceremony> = got(answer)
                let Some(c) = c else {
                    self.refuse(conn, expired(j.n))
                    return
                }
                if c.kind != j.n || c.expires < self.now {
                    self.refuse(conn, expired(j.n))
                    return
                }
                // A passkey added: begun by this account, in a session of its.
                if j.n == ADD_PASSKEY && c.account != j.id {
                    self.refuse(conn, expired(j.n))
                    return
                }
                // A new account: what it agreed to is still what it must (the versions may have
                // changed with the server since it began).
                if j.n == REGISTER {
                    if let Some(why) = self.disagreed(c.agreed) {
                        self.refuse(conn, why)
                        return
                    }
                    j.agreed = c.agreed
                }
                let (id, client_data, attestation) = match j.request.clone() {
                    Request::SignIn { id, .. } => {
                        j.message = c.challenge.clone()
                        self.get(passkey_key(id), Step::SignInCredential, take j)
                        return
                    },
                    Request::Register { id, client_data, attestation } => (
                        take id,
                        take client_data,
                        take attestation,
                    ),
                    Request::AddPasskey { id, client_data, attestation, .. } => (
                        take id,
                        take client_data,
                        take attestation,
                    ),
                    _ => return,
                }
                match registration(
                    id,
                    client_data,
                    attestation,
                    self.expected(c.challenge.clone()),
                ) {
                    Ok(cred) => {
                        j.credential = Some(cred.clone())
                        if j.n == REGISTER {
                            j.id = c.account
                            j.seed = c.seed
                            j.hash = c.handle.clone()
                            self.get(passkey_key(cred.id), Step::RegisterCredential, take j)
                        } else {
                            self.get(passkey_key(cred.id), Step::AddCredential, take j)
                        }
                    },
                    Err(why) => self.refuse(conn, why),
                }
            },
            Step::BeginAddScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                var exclude: Vec<Vec<u8>> = Vec::new()
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    exclude.push(part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip))
                }
                j.keys = take exclude
                self.get(account_key(j.id), Step::BeginAddAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::BeginAddAccount => {
                // A passkey added is made for the account's handle, as its first was.
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                j.hash = a.handle.clone()
                self.random(begin_bytes(ADD_PASSKEY), Step::BeginRandom, take j)
            },
            Step::RegisterCredential => {
                if value(answer).is_some() {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "That passkey already has an account. Sign in with it instead.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                self.get(account_key(j.id), Step::RegisterAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::RegisterAccount => {
                if value(answer).is_some() || j.id == 0 {
                    self.refuse(conn, "We couldn't make your account. Try again.")
                    return
                }
                let n = draw(j.seed)
                self.get(name_key(n), Step::RegisterName, take j)
            },
            Step::RegisterName | Step::NameTaken => {
                let n = draw(j.seed)
                if value(answer).is_some() || lately(self.recent_names, name_key(n)) {
                    // Taken: another draw, a few times.
                    j.tries += 1
                    if j.tries > 8 {
                        self.refuse(conn, "We couldn't find a name for you. Try again.")
                        return
                    }
                    let next = if j.step == Step::RegisterName { Step::RegisterSeed } else {
                        Step::NameSeed
                    }
                    self.random(8, next, take j)
                    return
                }
                if j.step == Step::RegisterName {
                    j.account = Some(
                        Account {
                            id: j.id,
                            handle: j.hash.clone(),
                            name: n,
                            fixed: false,
                            rerolls: REROLLS,
                            created: self.now,
                            deleting: false,
                        },
                    )
                    self.random(
                        TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES + CODES * CODE_BYTES,
                        Step::RegisterSecrets,
                        take j,
                    )
                } else {
                    self.renamed(take j, n)
                }
            },
            Step::RegisterSeed | Step::NameSeed => {
                if answer.len() < 8 {
                    return
                }
                j.seed = u64_at(answer, 0)
                let next = if j.step == Step::RegisterSeed { Step::RegisterName } else {
                    Step::NameTaken
                }
                self.get(name_key(draw(j.seed)), next, take j)
            },
            Step::RegisterSecrets => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(cred) = j.credential.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES + CODES * CODE_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                self.put(account_key(a.id), a.clone())
                self.put_bytes(name_key(a.name), save(a.id))
                self.recent_names.push((name_key(a.name), self.call))
                self.put(
                    passkey_key(cred.id),
                    Passkey {
                        account: a.id,
                        credential: cred.clone(),
                        created: self.now,
                        used: self.now,
                    },
                )
                self.put(
                    indexed(a.id, OF_PASSKEY, cred.id),
                    PasskeyView { id: cred.id.clone(), created: self.now, used: self.now },
                )
                self.put(agreement_key(a.id), Agreement { agreed: j.agreed, at: self.now })
                let codes = self.write_codes(
                    a.id,
                    part(answer, TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES, CODES * CODE_BYTES),
                )
                self.begin_session(conn, a, answer, recovery: false, codes: codes)
            },
            Step::SignInCredential => {
                let p: Option<Passkey> = got(answer)
                let removed = match j.request {
                    Request::SignIn { id, .. } => lately(self.gone, passkey_key(id)),
                    _ => false,
                }
                let p = if removed { None } else { take p }
                let Some(p) = p else {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "We don't know that passkey. Its account may have been deleted.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                j.passkey = Some(p.clone())
                self.get(account_key(p.account), Step::SignInAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::SignInAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey's account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                let Some(p) = j.passkey.clone() else { return }
                let Request::SignIn {
                    client_data,
                    authenticator_data,
                    signature,
                    user,
                    ..
                } = j.request.clone() else {
                    return
                }
                if a.deleting || p.account != a.id {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey's account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                // The browser names the account the passkey was made for: it must be this one.
                if !user.is_empty() && !same_bytes(user, a.handle) {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "That passkey belongs to another account. Sign in with it instead.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                match assertion(
                    client_data,
                    authenticator_data,
                    self.expected(j.message.clone()),
                    p.credential.clone(),
                ) {
                    Ok(signed) => {
                        j.account = Some(a.clone())
                        j.n = signed.counter
                        let t = self.next_ticket()
                        self.out.push(
                            Command::Verify {
                                ticket: t,
                                algorithm: p.credential.signature(),
                                key: p.credential.key.clone(),
                                message: signed.message.clone(),
                                signature,
                            },
                        )
                        j.ticket = t
                        j.step = Step::SignInVerify
                        self.push_job(take j)
                    },
                    Err(why) => self.refuse(conn, why),
                }
            },
            Step::SignInVerify => {
                if !verified(answer) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey's signature isn't valid. Try again.")
                    return
                }
                self.random(TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES, Step::SignInSecrets, take j)
            },
            Step::SignInSecrets => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(p) = j.passkey.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                // Removed (or its account deleted) while this sign-in went on.
                if lately(self.gone, passkey_key(p.credential.id)) {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "We don't know that passkey. Its account may have been deleted.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                var used = p.clone()
                used.credential.counter = j.n
                used.used = self.now
                self.put(passkey_key(p.credential.id), used.clone())
                self.put(
                    indexed(a.id, OF_PASSKEY, p.credential.id),
                    PasskeyView { id: p.credential.id.clone(), created: p.created, used: self.now },
                )
                self.begin_session(conn, a, answer, recovery: false, codes: Vec::new())
            },
            Step::RecoverCode => {
                let r: Option<Recovery> = got(answer)
                let r = if lately(self.gone, code_key(j.hash)) { None } else { take r }
                let Some(r) = r else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "We don't know that code, or it's already been used.")
                    return
                }
                j.id = r.account
                self.get(account_key(r.account), Step::RecoverAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::RecoverAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That code's account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                if a.deleting {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That code's account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                // Another request used it while this one read its account.
                if lately(self.gone, code_key(j.hash)) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "We don't know that code, or it's already been used.")
                    return
                }
                // Used up, and every other session ends.
                self.forget(code_key(j.hash))
                self.delete(indexed(a.id, OF_CODE, j.hash))
                j.account = Some(a.clone())
                self.scan(indexed(a.id, OF_SESSION, []), 256, Step::RecoverSessions, take j)
            },
            Step::RecoverSessions => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(a.id, OF_SESSION, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    let h = part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)
                    self.forget(session_key(h))
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                }
                self.unbind(a.id, Vec::new())
                self.random(TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES, Step::RecoverSecrets, take j)
            },
            Step::RecoverSecrets => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                self.begin_session(conn, a, answer, recovery: true, codes: Vec::new())
            },
            Step::NameAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                if a.fixed {
                    self.refuse(conn, "You've kept your name. It can't change now.")
                    return
                }
                match j.request {
                    Request::Keep { .. } => {
                        var kept = a.clone()
                        kept.fixed = true
                        self.put(account_key(a.id), kept.clone())
                        self.welcome(conn, me_of(kept, recovery: false))
                    },
                    _ => {
                        if a.rerolls == 0 {
                            self.refuse(conn, "You have no draws left.")
                            return
                        }
                        j.account = Some(a.clone())
                        self.random(8, Step::NameSeed, take j)
                    },
                }
            },
            Step::AddCredential => {
                if value(answer).is_some() {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey already has an account.")
                    return
                }
                self.scan(indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, []), MOST_PASSKEYS + 1, Step::AddCount, take j)
            },
            Step::AddCount => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                if es.len() >= MOST_PASSKEYS {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "An account has at most 16 passkeys. Remove one first.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                let Some(cred) = j.credential.clone() else { return }
                self.put(
                    passkey_key(cred.id),
                    Passkey { account: j.id, credential: cred.clone(), created: self.now, used: 0 },
                )
                self.put(
                    indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, cred.id),
                    PasskeyView { id: cred.id.clone(), created: self.now, used: 0 },
                )
                self.get(session_key(j.hash), Step::AddSession, take j)
            },
            Step::AddSession => {
                // A session a code made is a whole one once it has added a passkey.
                let s: Option<Session> = got(answer)
                if let Some(s) = s {
                    if s.recovery && !lately(self.gone, session_key(j.hash)) {
                        var whole = s.clone()
                        whole.recovery = false
                        whole.fresh_until = self.now + FRESH
                        self.put(session_key(j.hash), whole.clone())
                        self.bind(conn, j.hash.clone(), whole.clone())
                    }
                }
                self.get(account_key(j.id), Step::TokenAccount, take j)
                // TokenAccount with no game asked answers with the account, below.
            },
            Step::RemoveScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, []).len()
                var found = false
                var left: Vec<PasskeyView> = Vec::new()
                for e in es {
                    let id = part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)
                    if same_bytes(id, j.message) {
                        found = true
                    } else if let Some(v) = read::<PasskeyView>(e.value) {
                        left.push(take v)
                    }
                }
                if !found {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey isn't one of yours.")
                    return
                }
                if left.is_empty() {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "That's your only passkey. Add another before you remove it.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                self.forget(passkey_key(j.message))
                self.delete(indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, j.message))
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Passkeys { passkeys: left })
            },
            Step::PasskeysScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                var list: Vec<PasskeyView> = Vec::new()
                for e in es {
                    if let Some(v) = read::<PasskeyView>(e.value) {
                        list.push(take v)
                    }
                }
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Passkeys { passkeys: list })
            },
            Step::CodesScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_CODE, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    self.forget(code_key(part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)))
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                }
                self.random(CODES * CODE_BYTES, Step::CodesRandom, take j)
            },
            Step::CodesRandom => {
                if answer.len() < CODES * CODE_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                let codes = self.write_codes(j.id, answer)
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Codes { codes })
            },
            Step::SessionsScan | Step::RevokeScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_SESSION, []).len()
                var list: Vec<SessionView> = Vec::new()
                var revoked = false
                for e in es {
                    let h = part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)
                    let Some(v) = read::<SessionView>(e.value) else { continue }
                    if j.step == Step::RevokeScan && same_bytes(public_id(h), j.message) {
                        self.forget(session_key(h))
                        self.delete(e.key.clone())
                        self.unbind(j.id, h.clone())
                        revoked = true
                        continue
                    }
                    var view = v.clone()
                    view.this = same_bytes(h, j.hash)
                    list.push(take view)
                }
                if j.step == Step::RevokeScan && !revoked {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That session has already ended.")
                    return
                }
                if j.step == Step::RevokeScan && !self.is_signed_in(conn) {
                    // This session itself.
                    self.session_gone(conn)
                    self.welcome(conn, nobody())
                    return
                }
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Sessions { sessions: list })
            },
            Step::TokenAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                match j.request {
                    Request::Token { .. } => {
                        if !a.fixed {
                            self.refuse(conn, "Keep your name at the console first.")
                            return
                        }
                        j.account = Some(a.clone())
                        self.scan(indexed(a.id, OF_TOKEN, []), 64, Step::TokenPrune, take j)
                    },
                    // A passkey added: the account as it is now.
                    _ => {
                        let recovery = match self.conn_index(conn) {
                            Some(i) => self.conns[i].recovery,
                            None => false,
                        }
                        self.welcome(conn, me_of(a, recovery))
                    },
                }
            },
            Step::TokenPrune => {
                // Tokens that have expired go as a new one comes.
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(a.id, OF_TOKEN, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    if e.value.len() == 8 && u64_at(e.value, 0) < self.now {
                        self.delete(token_key(part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)))
                        self.delete(e.key.clone())
                    }
                }
                self.random(TOKEN_BYTES, Step::TokenRandom, take j)
            },
            Step::TokenRandom => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < TOKEN_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                let token = part(answer, 0, TOKEN_BYTES)
                var expires: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
                append_u64(mut expires, self.now + TOKEN_LIFE)
                self.put_bytes(indexed(a.id, OF_TOKEN, hashed(token)), take expires)
                self.put(
                    token_key(hashed(token)),
                    GameToken {
                        account: a.id,
                        game: String::from(self.game.id()),
                        expires: self.now + TOKEN_LIFE,
                    },
                )
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Token { token, expires_in: u32(TOKEN_LIFE / 1000) })
            },
            Step::ExportAccount => {
                // Where the last part ended: nowhere (the start), after a record, or after a
                // replay, each by its key (`export_part`).
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                let after = j.message.clone()
                // A cursor goes on within this account's records or runs, nowhere else.
                if !after.is_empty() {
                    let within = if after[0] == 0 { under_account(j.id) } else {
                        indexed(j.id, OF_RUN, [])
                    }
                    if after[0] > 1 || !starts_with(part(after, 1, after.len() - 1), within) {
                        self.refuse(conn, "That export can't continue from there. Start it again.")
                        return
                    }
                }
                if after.is_empty() {
                    j.text = export_head(a)
                    self.scan(under_account(j.id), EXPORT_RECORDS, Step::ExportScan, take j)
                } else if after[0] == 0 {
                    self.scan_after(
                        part(after, 1, after.len() - 1),
                        under_account(j.id),
                        EXPORT_RECORDS,
                        Step::ExportScan,
                        take j,
                    )
                } else {
                    j.n = 1
                    let runs = indexed(j.id, OF_RUN, [])
                    let from = part(after, 1, after.len() - 1)
                    self.scan_after(take from, runs, EXPORT_RUNS, Step::ExportRuns, take j)
                }
            },
            Step::ExportScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let prefix = under_account(j.id)
                for e in es {
                    if e.key.len() <= prefix.len() {
                        continue
                    }
                    let of = e.key[prefix.len()]
                    let rest = part(e.key, prefix.len() + 1, e.key.len() - prefix.len() - 1)
                    export_entry(mut j.text, of, rest, e.value)
                    if j.text.len() >= EXPORT_PART {
                        self.export_part(take j, 0, e.key.clone())
                        return
                    }
                }
                if es.len() == EXPORT_RECORDS {
                    borrow last = es[es.len() - 1].key
                    self.scan_after(last.clone(), prefix, EXPORT_RECORDS, Step::ExportScan, take j)
                    return
                }
                j.text.push_str("],\"replays\":[")
                j.n = 0
                self.scan(indexed(j.id, OF_RUN, []), EXPORT_RUNS, Step::ExportRuns, take j)
            },
            Step::ExportRuns => {
                // A batch of the account's runs, by their index keys, each read in turn.
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                j.keys.clear()
                j.views.clear()
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_RUN, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    if e.key.len() == skip + 8 {
                        j.keys.push(run_key(u64_at(e.key, skip)))
                        j.views.push(e.key.clone())
                    }
                }
                // Another batch follows a full one.
                j.tries = if es.len() == EXPORT_RUNS { 1 } else { 0 }
                self.export_next_run(take j)
            },
            Step::ExportRun => {
                let r: Option<Run> = got(answer)
                let at = j.views.remove(0)
                if let Some(r) = r {
                    if j.n > 0 {
                        j.text.push_str(",")
                    }
                    j.n += 1
                    j.text.push_str(f"{{\"run\":\"{r.id}\",\"replay\":\"{base64url(r.replay)}\"}}")
                }
                if j.text.len() >= EXPORT_PART {
                    self.export_part(take j, 1, take at)
                    return
                }
                j.hash = take at
                self.export_next_run(take j)
            },
            Step::DeleteAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    // A deletion resumed after it finished: only its mark is left. Others may wait.
                    self.delete(deletion_key(j.id))
                    self.deletion_written = self.call
                    self.deletions_waiting = true
                    return
                }
                var going = a.clone()
                going.deleting = true
                self.put(account_key(a.id), going.clone())
                // Marked, so a dropped instance's successor finishes it (`resume_deletions`).
                self.put_bytes(deletion_key(a.id), Vec::new())
                j.account = Some(take going)
                self.unbind(a.id, Vec::new())
                self.scan(under_account(a.id), 256, Step::DeleteScan, take j)
            },
            Step::DeleteNext => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                self.scan(under_account(a.id), 256, Step::DeleteScan, take j)
            },
            Step::DeleteScan => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                // A job of the account's may write after this scan, or wrote since it was made: the
                // deletion deletes nothing until none can, then scans afresh.
                if self.writing(a.id) {
                    self.random(1, Step::DeleteNext, take j)
                    return
                }
                let prefix = under_account(a.id)
                for e in es {
                    if e.key.len() <= prefix.len() {
                        continue
                    }
                    let of = e.key[prefix.len()]
                    let rest = part(e.key, prefix.len() + 1, e.key.len() - prefix.len() - 1)
                    if of == OF_PASSKEY {
                        self.forget(passkey_key(rest))
                    } else if of == OF_SESSION {
                        self.forget(session_key(rest))
                    } else if of == OF_CODE {
                        self.forget(code_key(rest))
                    } else if of == OF_TOKEN {
                        self.delete(token_key(rest))
                    } else if of == OF_RUN && rest.len() == 8 {
                        self.delete(run_key(u64_at(rest, 0)))
                    } else if of == OF_BEST {
                        if let Some(b) = best_of(e.value) {
                            self.delete(b.ranked.clone())
                        }
                    } else if of == OF_REPLAY {
                        // A hash it claimed: a copy another account uploaded was refused, so
                        // none of theirs goes with it.
                        self.forget(replay_key(rest))
                    }
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                }
                if es.len() == 256 {
                    // A scan now would be answered before these deletes commit, and find them
                    // again: the next is made in the next call, after a byte asked for.
                    self.random(1, Step::DeleteNext, take j)
                    return
                }
                self.delete(name_key(a.name))
                self.delete(posted_key(a.name))
                self.delete(account_key(a.id))
                self.delete(deletion_key(a.id))
                self.deletion_written = self.call
                if conn == 0 {
                    // Resumed: another may wait.
                    self.deletions_waiting = true
                }
                self.session_gone(conn)
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Done)
            },
            Step::DeleteResume => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                if es.is_empty() {
                    return
                }
                borrow e = es[0]
                if e.key.len() != deletions().len() + 8 {
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                    self.deletion_written = self.call
                    self.deletions_waiting = true
                    return
                }
                j.id = u64_at(e.key, deletions().len())
                self.get(account_key(j.id), Step::DeleteAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadToken => {
                let t: Option<GameToken> = got(answer)
                // What only stops it now (its token, its account, the queue, the hour) is refused,
                // so it's tried again; `Rejected` is for a run that can never go on the board.
                let Some(t) = t else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Sign in at the console to upload.")
                    return
                }
                if t.expires < self.now || t.game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Sign in at the console again to upload.")
                    return
                }
                for other in self.jobs {
                    if other.id == t.account && is_upload(other.step) {
                        self.refuse(conn, "One upload at a time. Wait for this one to finish.")
                        return
                    }
                }
                j.id = t.account
                self.get(account_key(t.account), Step::UploadAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                if a.deleting {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                // A board shows the name, so only a name that can't change goes on one.
                if !a.fixed {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Keep your name at the console first.")
                    return
                }
                j.account = Some(a.clone())
                self.get(posting_key(a.id), Step::UploadConsent, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadConsent => {
                // Posted only once the account agreed to what posting makes public.
                let p: Option<Posting> = got(answer)
                let agreed = match p {
                    Some(p) => p.version == self.versions.posting,
                    None => false,
                }
                if !agreed {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "Agree to what posting shares first. You're asked before your first post.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                j.hash = hashed(j.message)
                self.get(replay_key(j.hash), Step::UploadClaim, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadClaim => {
                // The replay uploaded before: what came of it, rather than another run.
                let u: Option<Uploaded> = got(answer)
                let u = if lately(self.gone, replay_key(j.hash)) { None } else { take u }
                let Some(j) = self.claimed(take j, take u) else { return }
                self.get(rate_key(j.id, self.now / HOUR), Step::UploadRate, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadPlace => {
                // A run verified before, posted again: its place now, counted as its first was.
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                self.reply(
                    conn,
                    Reply::Verified { run: j.seed, ticks: j.tries, place: es.len() + 1 },
                )
            },
            Step::UploadRate => {
                var count: u32 = 0
                if let Some(v) = value(answer) {
                    if v.len() == 4 {
                        count = u32_at(v, 0)
                    }
                }
                if count >= RUNS_AN_HOUR {
                    let why = String::from(
                        f"You can upload {RUNS_AN_HOUR} runs an hour. Try again later.",
                    )
                    self.reply(conn, Reply::Refused { why })
                    return
                }
                j.n = count
                self.scan(queue_prefix(), MOST_QUEUED + 1, Step::UploadQueue, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadQueue => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                // `tries` is the run's claimed ticks. The queue as read, and the uploads let in that
                // it couldn't count: those still to be written, and those written since it was read.
                var ticks = u64(j.tries)
                var runs = es.len()
                for e in es {
                    if let Some(q) = read::<Queued>(e.value) {
                        ticks += u64(q.ticks)
                    }
                }
                for other in self.jobs {
                    if other.step == Step::UploadId {
                        ticks += u64(other.tries)
                        runs += 1
                    }
                }
                let call = self.call
                self.admitted.retain(|a| a.0 + 1 >= call)
                for (_, t) in self.admitted {
                    ticks += u64(t)
                    runs += 1
                }
                if j.tries > QUEUE_TICKS {
                    // Longer than the queue holds: never taken.
                    let why = String::from("That run is too long to check.")
                    self.reply(conn, Reply::Rejected { why })
                    return
                }
                if runs >= MOST_QUEUED || ticks > u64(QUEUE_TICKS) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "The boards are busy. Try again in a few minutes.")
                    return
                }
                self.random(8, Step::UploadId, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadId => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < 8 {
                    return
                }
                // Claimed by another upload since this one's read: what came of that.
                let Some(j) = self.claimed(take j, None) else { return }
                // A run's number is never 0: 0 is a whole game's place.
                let id = max(u64_at(answer, 0), 1)
                let Request::Upload { replay, .. } = j.request.clone() else { return }
                var count: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
                append_u32(mut count, j.n + 1)
                self.put_bytes(rate_key(a.id, self.now / HOUR), take count)
                // The hash is the account's now, and its name one a search may find.
                self.put(
                    replay_key(j.hash),
                    Uploaded { account: a.id, run: id, checked: Checked::Waiting },
                )
                self.put_bytes(indexed(a.id, OF_REPLAY, j.hash), Vec::new())
                self.claims.push(
                    Claiming { hash: j.hash.clone(), call: self.call, account: a.id, run: id },
                )
                self.put_bytes(posted_key(a.name), save(a.id))
                let q = Queued {
                    id,
                    account: a.id,
                    name: names::text(a.name),
                    game: String::from(self.game.id()),
                    board: self.game.board(),
                    course: j.category,
                    ticks: j.tries,
                    uploaded: self.now,
                    replay: replay.clone(),
                }
                self.put(queue_key(self.now, id), q)
                self.admitted.push((self.call, j.tries))
                self.queue_waiting = true
                self.queue_written = self.call
                // Answered when its run is.
                if let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) {
                    self.conns[i].run = id
                }
            },
            Step::BoardScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let Request::Board { course, .. } = j.request.clone() else { return }
                var places: Vec<Place> = Vec::new()
                for k in j.n..min(es.len(), j.n + BOARD_PAGE) {
                    borrow e = es[k]
                    let Some(p) = place_of(e.key, e.value, k + 1, course) else { continue }
                    places.push(take p)
                }
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Board { places, total: es.len() })
            },
            Step::WatchRun => {
                let r: Option<Run> = got(answer)
                let Some(r) = r else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That run is gone.")
                    return
                }
                self.reply(
                    conn,
                    Reply::Run { run: r.id, game: r.game.clone(), replay: r.replay.clone() },
                )
            },
            Step::PostingRead => {
                let p: Option<Posting> = got(answer)
                j.n = if self.agreed_to(take p) { 1 } else { 0 }
                self.get(post_best_key(j.id), Step::PostingBest, take j)
            },
            Step::PostingBest => {
                // Off until chosen.
                let b: Option<PostBest> = got(answer)
                let best_runs = match b {
                    Some(b) => b.on,
                    None => false,
                }
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Posting { agreed: j.n == 1, best_runs })
            },
            Step::BestRunsRead => {
                let p: Option<Posting> = got(answer)
                let agreed = self.agreed_to(take p)
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Posting { agreed, best_runs: j.n == 1 })
            },
            Step::ReplayIndex => {
                // A verified run's, and only that.
                let u: Option<Uploaded> = got(answer)
                let run = match u {
                    Some(u) => match u.checked {
                        Checked::Verified { .. } => Some(u.run),
                        _ => None,
                    },
                    None => None,
                }
                let Some(run) = run else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That replay isn't on the boards.")
                    return
                }
                self.get(run_key(run), Step::ReplayRun, take j)
            },
            Step::ReplayRun => {
                // What the hash names, and only that: the bytes never change, so a cache keeps them.
                let r: Option<Run> = got(answer)
                let named = match r {
                    Some(r) => same_bytes(hashed(r.replay), j.hash),
                    None => false,
                }
                if !named {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That replay isn't on the boards.")
                    return
                }
                let Some(r) = r else { return }
                let reply = Reply::Run { run: r.id, game: r.game.clone(), replay: r.replay.clone() }
                self.respond(conn, take reply, REPLAY_AGE, immutable: true)
            },
            Step::AroundName => {
                let id: Option<u64> = got(answer)
                let Some(id) = id else {
                    self.reply(conn, Reply::Unplaced)
                    return
                }
                let Request::Around { game, course, category, .. } = j.request.clone() else {
                    return
                }
                j.id = id
                // The board's ranking, kept for each read of it.
                j.message = board_prefix(game, self.game.board(), course, category)
                self.get(
                    best_key(id, game, self.game.board(), course, category),
                    Step::AroundBest,
                    take j,
                )
            },
            Step::AroundBest => {
                let b = match value(answer) {
                    Some(v) => best_of(v),
                    None => None,
                }
                let Some(b) = b else {
                    self.reply(conn, Reply::Unplaced)
                    return
                }
                // Every place ahead of it, as many as are counted: how many, and the last of them
                // are the places just above.
                j.hash = b.ranked.clone()
                let from = j.message.clone()
                self.scan_range(take from, b.ranked.clone(), MOST_PLACE, Step::AroundCount, take j)
            },
            Step::AroundCount => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                if es.len() == MOST_PLACE {
                    // Past the places counted: those just above are read from it, unnumbered.
                    j.tries = 0
                    let from = j.message.clone()
                    self.scan_down(take from, j.hash.clone(), AROUND, Step::AroundAbove, take j)
                    return
                }
                j.tries = es.len() + 1
                for k in es.len() - min(AROUND, es.len())..es.len() {
                    j.keys.push(es[k].key.clone())
                    j.views.push(es[k].value.clone())
                }
                self.around_below(take j)
            },
            Step::AroundAbove => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                // The last first: kept fastest first.
                var k = es.len()
                while k > 0 {
                    k -= 1
                    j.keys.push(es[k].key.clone())
                    j.views.push(es[k].value.clone())
                }
                self.around_below(take j)
            },
            Step::AroundBelow => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let Request::Around { course, .. } = j.request.clone() else { return }
                // `tries` is its place, if within the places counted (0 if not), and `n` the places
                // above it in the slice: the slice's are numbered from it.
                let at = j.tries
                var places: Vec<Place> = Vec::new()
                for i in 0..j.keys.len() + es.len() {
                    let number = if at == 0 { 0 } else { at - j.n + i }
                    let p = if i < j.keys.len() {
                        place_of(j.keys[i], j.views[i], number, course)
                    } else {
                        borrow e = es[i - j.keys.len()]
                        place_of(e.key, e.value, number, course)
                    }
                    if let Some(p) = take p {
                        places.push(take p)
                    }
                }
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Around { places, at })
            },
            Step::NamesRange => self.names_range(take j, answer),
            Step::NamesAccount => self.names_account(take j, answer),
            Step::QueueAccount => {
                self.queue_scan = None
                let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let gone = match a {
                    Some(a) => a.deleting,
                    None => true,
                }
                if gone {
                    self.delete(j.keys[0].clone())
                    self.queue_written = self.call
                    self.tell(
                        q.id,
                        Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("That run's account is gone.") },
                    )
                    return
                }
                let run = self.game.start(q.replay)
                self.verifying = Some(Verifying { key: j.keys[0].clone(), queued: q.clone(), run })
            },
            Step::FinishBest => self.finish_best(take j, answer),
            Step::FinishBests => self.finish_bests(take j, answer),
            Step::FinishPlace => {
                let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                // The places ahead, and this one.
                let place = es.len() + 1
                self.tell(q.id, Reply::Verified { run: q.id, ticks: j.tries, place })
            },
        }
    }

    /// The slice's places above are read: then its own and those below it.
    fn around_below(mut self, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        j.n = j.keys.len()
        let to = past(j.message).unwrap_or(Vec::new())
        self.scan_range(j.hash.clone(), take to, AROUND + 1, Step::AroundBelow, take j)
    }

    /// An upload of a replay claimed before (`u`, as the store had it when `job` read it, or a
    /// claim made since): its own account hears what came of the first upload, once its run is
    /// played if it waits to be, and another account's copy is refused. `job` back if the replay
    /// is new.
    fn claimed(mut self, job: take Job, u: take Option<Uploaded>) -> Option<Job> {
        var j = take job
        let conn = j.conn
        var held = take u
        if held.is_none() {
            for c in self.claims {
                if same_bytes(c.hash, j.hash) {
                    held = Some(
                        Uploaded { account: c.account, run: c.run, checked: Checked::Waiting },
                    )
                }
            }
        }
        let Some(u) = take held else { return Some(take j) }
        if u.account != j.id {
            // A replay names one run. A copy of a rejected run would be rejected the same.
            let why = match u.checked {
                Checked::Rejected { why } => why.clone(),
                _ => String::from("That run is already on the boards."),
            }
            self.reply(conn, Reply::Rejected { why })
            return None
        }
        match u.checked {
            Checked::Waiting => {
                // Played since this read was asked: read what came of it.
                for (run, call) in self.finished {
                    if run == u.run && call >= j.asked {
                        let k = replay_key(j.hash)
                        self.get(take k, Step::UploadClaim, take j)
                        return None
                    }
                }
                if let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) {
                    self.conns[i].run = u.run
                }
            },
            Checked::Verified { board, course, ticks } => {
                j.seed = u.run
                j.tries = ticks
                let from = board_prefix(self.game.id(), board, course, ANY)
                let to = ranked_key(self.game.id(), board, course, ANY, ticks, u.account)
                self.scan_range(take from, take to, MOST_PLACE, Step::UploadPlace, take j)
            },
            Checked::Rejected { why } => self.reply(conn, Reply::Rejected { why: why.clone() }),
        }
        None
    }

    /// The upload of `q` is given up before it was played (its board's version is another): its
    /// hash is let go, so it may be uploaded again.
    fn unclaim(mut self, q: Queued) {
        let hash = hashed(q.replay)
        self.claims.retain(|c| !same_bytes(c.hash, hash))
        self.forget(replay_key(hash))
        self.delete(indexed(q.account, OF_REPLAY, hash))
    }

    /// Writes what came of upload `q`'s run (`Uploaded`).
    fn checked(mut self, q: Queued, checked: take Checked) {
        let hash = hashed(q.replay)
        self.put(replay_key(hash), Uploaded { account: q.account, run: q.id, checked })
        self.finished.push((q.id, self.call))
    }

    /// A page of one of a search's ranges of the name index: the names in it that match, then the
    /// range's next page, the next range, or the runs of the names found.
    fn names_range(mut self, job: take Job, answer: Vec<u8>) {
        var j = take job
        let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
        let Some(m) = j.matching else { return }
        let skip = text_key("p/").len()
        for e in es {
            j.tries += 1
            if e.key.len() != skip + 8 || j.views.len() >= MOST_CANDIDATES {
                continue
            }
            let Some(n) = names::from_key(part(e.key, skip, 8)) else { continue }
            let id: Option<u64> = read(e.value)
            let Some(id) = id else { continue }
            if names::matches(m, n) {
                // A candidate: its name's key, then its account's number.
                var c = part(e.key, skip, 8)
                append_u64(mut c, id)
                j.views.push(take c)
            }
        }
        let room = j.views.len() < MOST_CANDIDATES && j.tries < MOST_SCANNED
        if room && es.len() == RANGE_PAGE {
            var from = es[es.len() - 1].key.clone()
            from.push(0)
            let to = j.keys[1].clone()
            self.scan_range(take from, take to, RANGE_PAGE, Step::NamesRange, take j)
            return
        }
        let _ = j.keys.remove(0)
        let _ = j.keys.remove(0)
        if room && !j.keys.is_empty() {
            let (from, to) = (j.keys[0].clone(), j.keys[1].clone())
            self.scan_range(take from, take to, RANGE_PAGE, Step::NamesRange, take j)
            return
        }
        self.names_read(take j)
    }

    /// Reads every candidate's account and its bests at once, a scan each, or answers with none.
    fn names_read(mut self, job: take Job) {
        let j = take job
        if j.views.is_empty() {
            self.reply(j.conn, Reply::Names { found: Vec::new() })
            return
        }
        self.searching.push(Search { conn: j.conn, found: Vec::new(), left: j.views.len() })
        let to_end = self.game.courses() * 4 + 8
        for k in 0..j.views.len() {
            let id = u64_at(j.views[k], 8)
            var c = blank_job(j.conn, j.request.clone())
            c.since = j.since
            c.n = k
            c.views.push(j.views[k].clone())
            let to = past(bests_prefix(id, self.game.id(), self.game.board())).unwrap_or(Vec::new())
            self.scan_range(account_key(id), take to, to_end, Step::NamesAccount, take c)
        }
    }

    /// A candidate's account and its bests: found if it isn't being deleted and has a run on the
    /// boards, which is all a board shows of it. The search answers once its every candidate is
    /// read, with the first `MOST_FOUND` found in the index's order.
    fn names_account(mut self, job: take Job, answer: Vec<u8>) {
        let j = take job
        let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
        let id = u64_at(j.views[0], 8)
        let name = names::from_key(part(j.views[0], at: 0, n: 8))
        var live = false
        var standings: Vec<Standing> = Vec::new()
        let prefix = bests_prefix(id, self.game.id(), self.game.board())
        for e in es {
            if e.key == account_key(id) {
                if let Some(a) = read::<Account>(e.value) {
                    live = !a.deleting
                }
            } else if starts_with(e.key, prefix) && e.key.len() == prefix.len() + 8 {
                let Some(b) = best_of(e.value) else { continue }
                standings.push(
                    Standing {
                        course: u32_at(e.key, prefix.len()),
                        category: u32_at(e.key, prefix.len() + 4),
                        ticks: b.ticks,
                        run: b.run,
                        replay: b.replay.clone(),
                    },
                )
            }
        }
        var at: Option<u32> = None
        for i in 0..self.searching.len() {
            if self.searching[i].conn == j.conn {
                at = Some(i)
            }
        }
        // Its search refused already (another candidate's read failed).
        let Some(i) = at else { return }
        if let Some(n) = name {
            if live && !standings.is_empty() {
                self.searching[i].found.push((j.n, Found { name: names::text(n), standings }))
            }
        }
        self.searching[i].left -= 1
        if self.searching[i].left > 0 {
            return
        }
        var search = self.searching.remove(i)
        search.found.sort_by(|a, b| a.0 < b.0)
        var found: Vec<Found> = Vec::new()
        for (_, f) in search.found {
            if found.len() < MOST_FOUND {
                found.push(f.clone())
            }
        }
        self.reply(j.conn, Reply::Names { found })
    }

    /// A name drawn again: the old one let go, the new one the account's.
    fn renamed(mut self, job: take Job, n: Name) {
        let j = take job
        let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
        var b = a.clone()
        b.name = n
        b.rerolls = a.rerolls - 1
        self.delete(name_key(a.name))
        self.put_bytes(name_key(n), save(a.id))
        self.recent_names.push((name_key(n), self.call))
        self.put(account_key(a.id), b.clone())
        self.welcome(j.conn, me_of(b, recovery: false))
    }

    /// Answers with an export's part, which ended after the key `key` of its records (`phase` 0)
    /// or of its runs' index (1): the console asks for the next from there.
    fn export_part(mut self, job: take Job, phase: u8, key: take Vec<u8>) {
        var next = Vec::from([phase])
        with_bytes(mut next, key)
        self.reply(job.conn, Reply::Export { text: job.text.clone(), next, last: false })
    }

    /// Reads the next run of the batch, or the next batch after a full one, or ends the export.
    fn export_next_run(mut self, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        if !j.keys.is_empty() {
            let k = j.keys.remove(0)
            self.get(take k, Step::ExportRun, take j)
            return
        }
        if j.tries == 1 {
            let runs = indexed(j.id, OF_RUN, [])
            self.scan_after(j.hash.clone(), runs, EXPORT_RUNS, Step::ExportRuns, take j)
            return
        }
        j.text.push_str("]}")
        self.reply(j.conn, Reply::Export { text: j.text.clone(), next: Vec::new(), last: true })
    }

    /// Scans on from just after `key`, within `prefix`, `limit` entries at most.
    fn scan_after(
        mut self,
        key: take Vec<u8>,
        prefix: Vec<u8>,
        limit: u32,
        step: Step,
        job: take Job,
    ) {
        var from = take key
        from.push(0)
        let to = past(prefix).unwrap_or(Vec::new())
        self.scan_range(take from, take to, limit, step, take job)
    }

    // ---- verification -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    /// Plays the run being verified a call's share, or takes the oldest from the queue.
    fn verify_some(mut self) {
        var taken = replace(mut self.verifying, None)
        match mut taken {
            Some(v) => {
                match self.game.play(mut v.run, PLAY_TICKS) {
                    None => {
                        // More to play: something must call again.
                        self.nudge_next()
                        self.verifying = take taken
                    },
                    Some(result) => {
                        self.delete(v.key.clone())
                        self.queue_waiting = true
                        self.queue_written = self.call
                        self.played(v.queued.clone(), result)
                    },
                }
            },
            None => {
                if self.queue_waiting && self.queue_scan.is_none() {
                    if self.call <= self.queue_written {
                        // The queue was written this call: read it in the next, which a byte
                        // asked for brings at once.
                        self.nudge_next()
                        return
                    }
                    let t = self.next_ticket()
                    let from = queue_prefix()
                    let to = past(from).unwrap_or(Vec::new())
                    self.out.push(Command::Scan { ticket: t, from, to, limit: 1, down: false })
                    self.queue_scan = Some(t)
                }
            },
        }
    }

    /// Finishes a deletion a dropped instance left, one at a time: looked for when the engine starts
    /// and after each it finishes, once that finish has committed.
    fn resume_deletions(mut self) {
        if !self.deletions_waiting || self.call <= self.deletion_written {
            return
        }
        self.deletions_waiting = false
        self.scan(deletions(), 1, Step::DeleteResume, blank_job(0, Request::Me))
    }

    /// Lets go of what was deleted or written lately once no read made before it can still be
    /// used: kept while a job that began by then is under way, and for the call after (a read made
    /// in a call is answered in the next).
    fn forget_old(mut self) {
        var oldest = self.call
        for j in self.jobs {
            oldest = min(oldest, j.since)
        }
        let call = self.call
        self.gone.retain(|g| g.1 >= oldest || g.1 + 1 >= call)
        self.recent_names.retain(|g| g.1 >= oldest || g.1 + 1 >= call)
        self.claims.retain(|c| c.call >= oldest || c.call + 1 >= call)
        self.finished.retain(|f| f.1 >= oldest || f.1 + 1 >= call)
        self.touched.retain(|t| t.1 + 1 >= call)
    }

    /// Whether a job may still write account `account`'s records, or did in this call or the last:
    /// a deletion deletes nothing while one might (it would miss what that writes).
    fn writing(self, account: u64) -> bool {
        for (a, _) in self.touched {
            if a == account {
                return true
            }
        }
        // A run of the account's being uploaded, verified, or ranked once played.
        if let Some(v) = self.verifying {
            if v.queued.account == account {
                return true
            }
        }
        for j in self.jobs {
            if is_upload(j.step) && j.id == account {
                return true
            }
            if let Some(q) = j.queued {
                if q.account == account {
                    return true
                }
            }
        }
        false
    }

    /// Asks the host for a byte, so that it calls again at once (the host calls while answers
    /// arrive).
    fn nudge_next(mut self) {
        if self.nudge.is_none() {
            let t = self.next_ticket()
            self.out.push(Command::Random { ticket: t, n: 1 })
            self.nudge = Some(t)
        }
    }

    fn queue_answered(mut self, answer: Option<Vec<u8>>) {
        let Some(bytes) = answer else { return }
        let Some(es) = entries(bytes) else { return }
        if es.is_empty() {
            self.queue_waiting = false
            return
        }
        borrow e = es[0]
        let Some(q) = read::<Queued>(e.value) else {
            // What can't be read can't be verified.
            self.delete(e.key.clone())
            self.queue_written = self.call
            return
        }
        if q.board != self.game.board() || q.game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
            self.delete(e.key.clone())
            self.unclaim(q)
            self.queue_written = self.call
            self.tell(
                q.id,
                Reply::Rejected {
                    why: String::from("That run is for another version of the game."),
                },
            )
            return
        }
        // A run whose account went while it waited goes with it.
        var job = blank_job(0, Request::Watch { run: q.id })
        job.queued = Some(q.clone())
        job.keys.push(e.key.clone())
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Get { ticket: t, key: account_key(q.account) })
        job.ticket = t
        job.step = Step::QueueAccount
        self.push_job(take job)
        self.queue_scan = Some(0)
    }

    /// A run played to its end: refused, or kept and ranked.
    fn played(mut self, q: Queued, result: Result<Outcome, Text>) {
        self.touched.push((q.account, self.call))
        match result {
            Err(why) => {
                self.checked(q, Checked::Rejected { why: String::from(why) })
                self.tell(q.id, Reply::Rejected { why: String::from(why) })
            },
            Ok(o) => {
                if o.ticks != q.ticks {
                    let why = String::from("That run's time doesn't match its moves.")
                    self.checked(q, Checked::Rejected { why: why.clone() })
                    self.tell(q.id, Reply::Rejected { why })
                    return
                }
                let r = Run {
                    id: q.id,
                    account: q.account,
                    game: q.game.clone(),
                    board: q.board,
                    course: q.course,
                    ticks: o.ticks,
                    full: o.full,
                    uploaded: q.uploaded,
                    replay: q.replay.clone(),
                }
                self.put(run_key(r.id), r.clone())
                var id8: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
                append_u64(mut id8, r.id)
                // Its replay by its hash, a public read now.
                self.checked(
                    q,
                    Checked::Verified { board: r.board, course: r.course, ticks: r.ticks },
                )
                self.put(
                    indexed(r.account, OF_RUN, id8),
                    RunIndex {
                        game: r.game.clone(),
                        board: r.board,
                        course: r.course,
                        ticks: r.ticks,
                        full: r.full,
                        uploaded: r.uploaded,
                    },
                )
                var job = blank_job(0, Request::Watch { run: r.id })
                job.queued = Some(q.clone())
                job.tries = o.ticks
                job.categories.push(ANY)
                if o.full {
                    job.categories.push(FULL)
                }
                self.next_best(take job)
            },
        }
    }

    /// The next category of the finished run: read the account's best there.
    fn next_best(mut self, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
        if j.categories.is_empty() {
            // Ranked: its place on the any% board.
            let from = board_prefix(q.game, q.board, q.course, ANY)
            let to = ranked_key(q.game, q.board, q.course, ANY, j.tries, q.account)
            self.scan_range(take from, take to, MOST_PLACE, Step::FinishPlace, take j)
            return
        }
        j.category = j.categories.remove(0)
        self.get(
            best_key(q.account, q.game, q.board, q.course, j.category),
            Step::FinishBest,
            take j,
        )
    }

    fn finish_best(mut self, job: take Job, answer: Vec<u8>) {
        let j = take job
        let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
        let old = match value(answer) {
            Some(v) => best_of(v),
            None => None,
        }
        if let Some(b) = old {
            if b.ticks <= j.tries {
                // Not better than the account's best.
                self.next_best(take j)
                return
            }
            self.delete(b.ranked.clone())
        }
        let ranked = ranked_key(q.game, q.board, q.course, j.category, j.tries, q.account)
        let replay = hashed(q.replay)
        self.put(ranked.clone(), Ranked { name: q.name.clone(), run: q.id, replay: replay.clone() })
        self.put(
            best_key(q.account, q.game, q.board, q.course, j.category),
            Best { run: q.id, ticks: j.tries, ranked, replay },
        )
        // A new best changes the whole game's sum: read every best of the account's.
        self.scan(
            bests_prefix(q.account, q.game, q.board),
            4 * self.game.courses() + 4,
            Step::FinishBests,
            take j,
        )
    }

    fn finish_bests(mut self, job: take Job, answer: Vec<u8>) {
        let j = take job
        let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
        let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
        // The bests the scan saw are as of before this call's writes: the one just written is
        // this run's.
        var courses: Vec<u32> = Vec::new()
        var sum: u32 = 0
        var whole_old: Option<Best> = None
        let skip = bests_prefix(q.account, q.game, q.board).len()
        for e in es {
            if e.key.len() < skip + 8 {
                continue
            }
            let course = u32_at(e.key, skip)
            let category = u32_at(e.key, skip + 4)
            if category != j.category {
                continue
            }
            let Some(b) = best_of(e.value) else { continue }
            if course == WHOLE {
                whole_old = Some(take b)
            } else if course != q.course {
                courses.push(course)
                sum += b.ticks
            }
        }
        courses.push(q.course)
        sum += j.tries
        if courses.len() == self.game.courses() {
            if let Some(b) = whole_old {
                self.delete(b.ranked.clone())
            }
            let ranked = whole_key(q.game, q.board, j.category, sum, q.account)
            self.put(ranked.clone(), Ranked { name: q.name.clone(), run: 0, replay: Vec::new() })
            self.put(
                best_key(q.account, q.game, q.board, WHOLE, j.category),
                Best { run: 0, ticks: sum, ranked, replay: Vec::new() },
            )
        }
        self.next_best(take j)
    }
}

/// The place numbered `number` on a board of `course` from its ranking's entry (`key`, `value`): the
/// key ends with the time and the account.
fn place_of(key: [u8], value: [u8], number: u32, course: u32) -> Option<Place> {
    let r = ranked_of(value)?
    if key.len() < 12 {
        return None
    }
    let whole = course == WHOLE
    Some(
        Place {
            place: number,
            name: r.name.clone(),
            ticks: u32_at(key, key.len() - 12),
            run: if whole { 0 } else { r.run },
            replay: if whole { Vec::new() } else { r.replay.clone() },
        },
    )
}

/// `p/<title><front>`: where the names of title `title` and first half `front` start in the index
/// of names on the boards (`account::posted_key`'s), each part two bytes, big-endian.
fn name_index(title: u32, front: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = text_key("p/")
    for p in [title, front] {
        k.push(u8(p >> 8))
        k.push(u8(p & 255))
    }
    k
}

/// Whether `part` can be the start of a part of a name: at most `MOST_PART` bytes of letters,
/// spaces and hyphens.
fn searchable(part: str) -> bool {
    if part.len() > MOST_PART {
        return false
    }
    for i in 0..part.len() {
        if !names::name_char(part.byte(i)) {
            return false
        }
    }
    true
}

/// Whether `bytes` starts with `prefix`.
fn starts_with(bytes: [u8], prefix: [u8]) -> bool {
    if bytes.len() < prefix.len() {
        return false
    }
    for i in 0..prefix.len() {
        if bytes[i] != prefix[i] {
            return false
        }
    }
    true
}

/// Whether `key` is among the keys used lately.
fn lately(keys: [(Vec<u8>, u64)], key: [u8]) -> bool {
    for (k, _) in keys {
        if same_bytes(k, key) {
            return true
        }
    }
    false
}

/// Whether `r` is no session's: a public read, or an upload, which a game's token makes.
fn sessionless(r: Request) -> bool {
    match r {
        Request::Upload { .. } => true,
        _ => public(r),
    }
}

/// The random bytes a ceremony of `kind` begins with: its challenge and its browser's token, and for
/// a new account, its handle, number and name's seed.
fn begin_bytes(kind: u32) -> u32 {
    let n = CHALLENGE_BYTES + CEREMONY_BYTES
    if kind == REGISTER { n + HANDLE_BYTES + 16 } else { n }
}

/// Why a ceremony of `kind` can't be finished: it has expired, or was used.
fn expired(kind: u32) -> Text {
    if kind == REGISTER {
        "That sign-up has expired. Start again."
    } else if kind == SIGN_IN { "That sign-in has expired. Try again." } else {
        "That has expired. Start again."
    }
}

/// Drops the times in `xs` older than `window` before `now`.
fn recent(xs: mut Vec<u64>, now: u64, window: u64) {
    var i = 0
    while i < xs.len() {
        if xs[i] + window <= now {
            let _ = xs.remove(i)
        } else {
            i += 1
        }
    }
}

fn is_deletion(step: Step) -> bool {
    step == Step::DeleteAccount ||
        step == Step::DeleteScan ||
        step == Step::DeleteNext ||
        step == Step::DeleteResume
}

fn is_upload(step: Step) -> bool {
    step == Step::UploadAccount ||
        step == Step::UploadConsent ||
        step == Step::UploadClaim ||
        step == Step::UploadRate ||
        step == Step::UploadQueue ||
        step == Step::UploadId
}

/// A whole game's board: `b/<board>` with `WHOLE` for its course.
pub fn whole_prefix(game: str, board: u32, category: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    board_prefix(game, board, WHOLE, category)
}

pub fn whole_key(game: str, board: u32, category: u32, ticks: u32, account: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    ranked_key(game, board, WHOLE, category, ticks, account)
}

// ---- the export ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn quoted(out: mut String, s: str) {
    out.push_str("\"")
    json_text(mut out, s)
    out.push_str("\"")
}

fn export_head(a: Account) -> String {
    var out = String::from(
        "{\"about\":\"Everything wrela.dev keeps about your account. Times are in milliseconds, on the server's clock.\",",
    )
    out.push_str(f"\"account\":{{\"id\":\"{a.id}\",\"handle\":\"{base64url(a.handle)}\",\"name\":")
    quoted(mut out, names::text(a.name).as_str())
    out.push_str(f",\"name_fixed\":{a.fixed},\"created\":{a.created}}},\"records\":[")
    out
}

/// One of an account's index entries as JSON, after the ones before it.
fn export_entry(out: mut String, of: u8, rest: [u8], value: [u8]) {
    if !out.ends_with("[") {
        out.push_str(",")
    }
    if of == OF_PASSKEY {
        let v = read::<PasskeyView>(value)
        out.push_str(f"{{\"passkey\":\"{base64url(rest)}\"")
        if let Some(v) = v {
            out.push_str(f",\"created\":{v.created},\"used\":{v.used}")
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_SESSION {
        let v = read::<SessionView>(value)
        out.push_str(f"{{\"session\":\"{hex(public_id(rest))}\"")
        if let Some(v) = v {
            out.push_str(f",\"created\":{v.created},\"seen\":{v.seen}")
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_CODE {
        out.push_str("{\"recovery_code\":\"unused (we keep only its hash)\"}")
    } else if of == OF_RUN {
        let v = read::<RunIndex>(value)
        let id = if rest.len() == 8 { u64_at(rest, 0) } else { 0 }
        out.push_str(f"{{\"run\":\"{id}\"")
        if let Some(v) = v {
            out.push_str(",\"game\":")
            quoted(mut out, v.game.as_str())
            out.push_str(
                f",\"board\":{v.board},\"course\":{v.course},\"ticks\":{v.ticks},\"full\":{v.full},\"uploaded\":{v.uploaded}",
            )
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_BEST {
        let v = best_of(value)
        out.push_str("{\"best\":")
        match v {
            Some(b) => out.push_str(f"{{\"run\":\"{b.run}\",\"ticks\":{b.ticks}}}"),
            None => out.push_str("null"),
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_TOKEN {
        out.push_str("{\"game_token\":\"(we keep only its hash, until it expires)\"}")
    } else if of == OF_HOUR {
        out.push_str("{\"uploads_this_hour\":\"(a count, for the upload limit)\"}")
    } else if of == OF_REPLAY {
        out.push_str(f"{{\"uploaded_replay_sha256\":\"{hex(rest)}\"}}")
    } else if of == OF_AGREED {
        out.push_str("{\"agreed\":")
        match read::<Agreement>(value) {
            Some(g) => out.push_str(
                f"{{\"terms\":{g.agreed.terms},\"privacy\":{g.agreed.privacy},\"thirteen_or_older\":{g.agreed.of_age},\"at\":{g.at}}}",
            ),
            None => out.push_str("null"),
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_POSTING {
        out.push_str("{\"posting\":")
        match read::<Posting>(value) {
            Some(p) => out.push_str(f"{{\"agreed_version\":{p.version},\"at\":{p.at}}}"),
            None => out.push_str("null"),
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_POST_BEST {
        out.push_str("{\"post_best_runs\":")
        match read::<PostBest>(value) {
            Some(b) => out.push_str(f"{{\"on\":{b.on},\"at\":{b.at}}}"),
            None => out.push_str("null"),
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else {
        out.push_str("{}")
    }
}
